window.FT_DAY_DECKS = {"1":{"day":1,"title":"VA Essentials","heading":"DAY 1 VA Essentials","slides":[{"id":"reading","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<p>A. Read the material below to get a good grasp of what we do here in the firm.</p>\n<h2 class=\"ftdd-pi-h\">Personal Injury</h2>\n<p>Personal injury law (also known as \"tort\" law) lets an injured person get compensation when someone else's wrongful conduct (negligence or an intentional act) causes harm. There are a variety of situations that can give rise to a valid personal injury claim, but remember that an injury doesn't automatically result in legal liability. Let's look at some of the most common kinds of personal injury cases.</p>\n<h3>Car Accident Cases</h3>\n<p>Car accidents spur the most personal injury cases in the United States. When an accident happens, usually it's because someone isn't following the rules of the road, or isn't driving as carefully as he or she should be. A careless driver can (usually) be held financially and responsible for injuries stemming from a car accident. Exceptions do exist in the dozen or so \"no fault\" states, where drivers have to collect from their own insurers except in cases of \"serious\" injury. Learn more about car accident injury cases.</p>\n<h3>Slip and Fall Cases</h3>\n<p>Slip and fall claims are another common type of personal injury case. Property owners (or, in some cases, those who are renting property) have a legal duty to keep their premises reasonably safe and free of hazards, so that people who are on the property do not become injured. Of course, not all injuries that occur on the property will lead to liability. The exact nature of a landowner's legal duty varies depending on the situation and according to the law in place in the state where the injury occurred.</p>\n<h3>Medical Malpractice</h3>\n<p>A medical malpractice claim can arise when a doctor or other health care professional provides treatment that falls below the appropriate medical standard of care, and a patient is injured as a result. But it's important to keep in mind that getting a bad result in the treatment setting doesn't mean malpractice occurred.</p>\n<p>Learn more about when it's medical malpractice (and when it isn't) and why medical malpractice cases are tough to win.</p>\n<h3>Defamation: Libel and Slander</h3>\n<p>Defamation in the form of libel or slander refers to an injury to a person's reputation as a result of untrue statements. The exact nature of what a defamation plaintiff must prove will vary depending on who the plaintiff is, and the forum where the statement was made. The average person usually just needs to prove that an untrue negative statement was made and that actual harm (financial loss) came from it. Celebrities or public figures, on the other hand, usually need to prove \"actual malice.\" This means they need to prove that the untrue statement was made either intentionally or with reckless disregard to the truth of the statement. Learn more about the legal elements of libel and slander.</p>\n<h3>Dog Bites</h3>\n<p>In most cases, the owners of a dog are financially responsible for bites and other injuries caused by the dog. The exact laws on owner responsibility vary from state to state, though. In some cases, strict liability rules exist and the dog owner is going to be liable for dog bite damages even if the dog has never shown any aggression or propensity to bite in the past. In other states, \"one bite\" rules exist, in which owners only become responsible for personal injury damages once there is a reason for those owners to know their dog is aggressive or prone to biting (like a previous history of bites.) Learn more about \"one bite\" versus \"strict\" liability in dog bite cases.</p>\n"},{"id":"reading-2","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<h3>Assault, Battery and Other Intentional Torts</h3>\n<p>Unlike most other types of personal injury claims, intentional torts are not based on accidents caused by negligence or carelessness, but rather when one person harms or injures another on purpose. These cases can involve the added aspect of a criminal case against the perpetrator. For example, when one person physically attacks another, he or she may face criminal charges. Additionally, the victim can file a personal injury lawsuit in civil court and demand compensation for injuries resulting from the attack. Learn more about intentional torts.</p>\n<h2 class=\"ftdd-pi-h\">Personal Injury Case Timeline</h2>\n<p>If you've been injured in any kind of accident that looks like it was someone else's fault, you might be wondering what to expect in a typical personal injury case, including how long it takes. This article will walk you through the standard timeline of a personal injury claim. (Important note: As you read, keep in mind that most personal injury cases settle, often without a lawsuit being filed in court. So your case probably won't reach every stage discussed here; it could settle at any point on the timeline.)</p>\n<h3>Step 1 - Get Medical Treatment</h3>\n<p>The first thing that you should do after getting injured in an accident is get medical treatment. That means, if you have even the slightest sense that you are hurt, go to the emergency room or make an appointment to see your doctor. Not only is this the right thing to do for your health, but, if you don’t see a doctor for some time after an accident, the insurance adjuster and the jury will probably assume that your injuries aren't that serious.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 2 - Consult a Personal Injury Lawyer</h3>\n<p>For anything more than a very minor claim, it's usually a good idea to at least discuss your situation with a personal injury lawyer. You can handle a small personal injury claim yourself (as long as you're comfortable with the process and confident you can get a fair result), but you will absolutely need a lawyer for any personal injury claim where you suffered significant injury, or the other side is putting up a fight on key issues. In general, if you are out of work for more than a couple of days, if you break a bone, or if your medical bills total more than a couple of thousand dollars, you should talk to a lawyer, and you might want to meet several of them. Get details on what to ask before hiring a personal injury lawyer.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 3 - Lawyer Investigates Claim and Reviews Medical Records</h3>\n<p>One of the first things your lawyer will do is interview you. The lawyer wants to know everything you know about the accident, your injuries, and your medical treatment. Lawyers don’t want to be surprised, so make sure to answer all questions as completely as you can.</p>\n<p>Next, the lawyer will get all of your medical records and bills relating to the injury and will probably also get your medical records for any treatment you have ever had relating to the condition at issue in the case. This can take months.</p>\n</div></div>\n"},{"id":"reading-3","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 4 - Lawyer Considers Making Demand and Negotiating</h3>\n<p>Many smaller personal injury claims are settled before a lawsuit is ever filed. If the lawyer thinks that the case can be settled, they will make a demand to the other attorney or the other side's insurance company. Learn more about how the settlement negotiation process works in a personal injury case.</p>\n<p>A good lawyer will not make a demand until the plaintiff has reached a point of maximum medical improvement (MMI). MMI is when the plaintiff has ended all medical treatment and is as recovered as possible. This is because, until the plaintiff has reached MMI, the lawyer does not know how much the case is worth. The lawyer should also not file a lawsuit until MMI. This is because, if the plaintiff is not at MMI by the time that the case goes to trial, the jury might undervalue the case.</p>\n<p>If settlement talks stall or the two sides are two far apart, the case moves into the \"litigation\" phase.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 5 - The Personal Injury Lawsuit is Filed</h3>\n<p>The litigation phase starts when you and your lawyer file a personal injury lawsuit in court. The filing of the lawsuit starts the clock running on when the case might get to trial. Every state’s pretrial procedures are different, but generally it will take one to two years for a personal injury case to get to trial. Keep in mind that a lawsuit needs to be filed within strict time limits that every state has set in a law called a statute of limitations.</p>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 6 - The Discovery Phase of a Personal Injury Case</h3>\n<p>The discovery phase is when each party investigates what the other side's legal claims and defenses are. They send interrogatories (a fancy word for questions) and document requests to each other, and take depositions of all relevant parties and witnesses, generally beginning with the plaintiff and defendant. This process can last six months to a year, depending on the court’s deadlines and the complexity of the case.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 7 - Mediation and Negotiation</h3>\n<p>As the discovery period ends, the lawyers will generally start talking settlement. Sometimes the lawyers can settle just by talking among themselves, but, in other cases, they will go to mediation, a process in which both clients and both lawyers get help from a neutral third party mediator to try to resolve the case. (Learn more about mediation of personal injury claims.)</p>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Step 8 - Trial</h3>\n<p>Mediation often works, but if it doesn’t, the case is scheduled for trial. A personal injury trial can last a day, a week, or even longer. The length may be increased because, in many states, trials are held for only half a day instead of over a full day. That doubles the length of a trial, but also lets the lawyers and judges get other things done in the afternoon.</p>\n<p>One important thing to know about trials is that just because a lawsuit is scheduled for trial does not mean the trial will actually occur on that date. Trials often get pushed because of the judge’s schedule. If your trial gets moved, you should not automatically assume that something unfavorable is happening. Trials are delayed all the time, and for the most innocuous of reasons. For details on this stage of the process in the context of one of the most common types of injury cases, learn what happens when a car accident case goes to trial.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Jury Selection in a Car Accident Trial</h3>\n<p>In most states, a jury (as opposed to a judge) decides the key issues in a car accident case. The jury is typically comprised of twelve persons, but sometimes that number can be lower.</p>\n<p>The first stage of the trial is called voir dire, and it is during this stage that the jury members are selected. In this phase potential jurors are asked a series of questions so that the lawyers and the judge can learn more about them. The purpose of the questions is to determine if the person has any biases or prejudices that might keep them from being fair and impartial.</p>\n</div></div>\n"},{"id":"reading-4","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<h2 class=\"ftdd-pi-h\">How Much Can I Get for My Personal Injury Case and How Long Will It Take?</h2>\n<p>You may be thinking of filing a personal injury claim after being hurt in a car accident, a slip-and-fall, or another incident caused by someone else’s carelessness. If so, you probably have lots of questions: What are my chances of getting fair compensation for my medical bills and other losses? Is it better to hire a lawyer, or can I handle it on my own? Is there anything I can do to increase my chances of success? How long will the process take?</p>\n<p>To help get answers to these and other pressing questions, we surveyed our readers across the United States and asked about their recent experiences with personal injury claims. Here’s what we learned.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Settlements: The Most Common Outcome in Personal Injury Claims</h3>\n<p>Overall, 70% of our readers with a personal injury claim received a payout (an out-of-court settlement or an award after a trial). And for nearly that many (67%), the compensation came in the form of a settlement. Very few readers (4%) saw their case go to trial, which is typical in personal injury cases. Trials can be time consuming, expensive, and risky for everyone involved. That’s why insurance adjusters—as well as the lawyers helping injured people—are usually motivated to reach a personal injury settlement.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/outcomes-chart.webp\" alt=\"Personal Injury Outcomes: 67% received settlement, 4% went to trial, 29% no trial or settlement.\" width=\"335\" height=\"340\"><img class=\"ftdd-pi-legend\" src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/outcomes-legend.webp\" alt=\"Received settlement, went to trial, no trial or settlement. More than two-thirds of readers received a settlement for their personal injury claims.\" width=\"335\" height=\"135\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>How Much Compensation Is Typical in Personal Injury Cases?</h3>\n<p>More than half of our readers received payouts ranging from just $3,000 to $25,000. But another 26% of readers received over $25,000, making the overall average $52,900. When you’re looking at these results, keep in mind that the readers we surveyed had come to our websites to find information about a claim and to look for a lawyer. It may be that those with the most severe injuries (which lead to a higher settlement or award) immediately retained a lawyer and therefore did not participate in our survey.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/payouts.webp\" alt=\"How Much Did Readers Receive? Less than $3,000: 16%. $3,000 to $10,000: 37%. $10,001 to $25,000: 21%. $25,001 to $75,000: 10%. More than $75,000: 16%.\" width=\"335\" height=\"475\"></figure></div></div>\n"},{"id":"reading-5","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<h3>What Affects the Outcome in Personal Injury Claims?</h3>\n<p>There tend to be general patterns as to how insurance companies value an injury case. You don’t have control over some factors that affect those patterns, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your injuries. Serious injuries result in more medical expenses and significant \"pain and suffering\" damages—which generally lead to higher payouts.</li>\n<li>The defendant’s insurance policy. Obviously, the insurance company won’t offer settlements over the policy limits.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>However, our survey results point to several things you can do that significantly affect the likelihood of a successful outcome as well as the amount of compensation you might receive: hiring a lawyer, negotiating settlement (rather than simply taking the first offer), and taking steps to involve the court.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>The Advantage of Legal Representation</h3>\n<p>Our survey showed that hiring a personal injury lawyer is the most important step you can take to increase your chances of getting compensation for your harm. More than nine out of ten readers who had legal representation received a settlement or award, compared to about half of those who proceeded on their own.</p>\n<p>Legal representation also made a big difference in the amount of personal injury payouts. Readers who hired a lawyer walked away with an average of $77,600 in compensation, compared to an average of $17,600 for those who handled their own injury claims.</p>\n<p>When we combine the survey results on compensation and attorneys’ fees, it’s clear that readers who hired lawyers still came out far ahead.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/lawyer-outcomes.webp\" alt=\"Effect of Lawyer on Outcomes: received payout with a lawyer 91%, received payout without a lawyer 51%\" width=\"303\" height=\"125\"></figure><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/lawyer-compensation.webp\" alt=\"Effect of Lawyer on Average Compensation: with a lawyer $77.6K, without a lawyer $17.6K\" width=\"280\" height=\"88\"></figure></div></div>\n<p>After deducting the average 32% contingency fee reported by our readers, they ended up with net payouts that were nearly three times higher, on average, than what unrepresented readers received. These results aren’t surprising. Lawyers know what it takes to build a solid personal injury claim, gather evidence, and deal with insurance adjusters. Learn more about when you need a personal injury lawyer and how to find the best personal injury lawyer for you and your case.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Negotiating Settlement Offers</h3>\n<p>It may seem obvious that you’ll end up with a higher settlement by negotiating rather than simply accepting the first offer from the other side. This may not be true in every case, but it’s still one of the most effective strategies for getting more money. Most of our readers (70%) held out for a better deal. As a result, they received settlements that were $30,700 higher, on average, compared to those who accepted the insurance company’s first offer. Get tips on negotiating a fair personal injury settlement.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/negotiation.webp\" alt=\"Effect of Negotiation on Average Settlement: accepted first offer $11.8K, negotiated $42.5K\" width=\"282\" height=\"88\"></figure></div></div>\n"},{"id":"reading-6","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Filing or Threatening a Personal Injury Lawsuit</h3>\n<p>Just over half of our readers settled or otherwise resolved their personal injury claims without filing a personal injury lawsuit or even notifying the other side that they were ready to do that. But readers who did take one of those steps were more likely to receive a settlement or award, and their payouts were almost twice as high as those who didn’t file or threaten lawsuits ($45,500 compared to $23,000).</p>\n<p>Even though most personal injury cases settle, and trials are rare, insurance companies are clearly more inclined to make a reasonable settlement offer if you show them that you’re serious by moving ahead toward a lawsuit.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/lawsuit.webp\" alt=\"Average Settlements and Court Involvement: filed/threatened lawsuit $45.5K, no steps toward lawsuit $23K\" width=\"300\" height=\"88\"></figure></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>How Long Does It Take to Resolve Personal Injury Claims?</h3>\n<p>Half of our readers resolved their personal injury claims within two months to a year, while 30% of readers waited over a year for their cases to be resolved. The overall average was 11.4 months. It’s natural to want a quick payout, but a faster resolution doesn’t necessarily mean a better result.</p>\n<p>For one thing, it took longer to resolve claims that had a successful outcome—a settlement or court award—than those that didn’t. Also, many of the factors that increased the likelihood of successful outcomes and higher payouts also increased the average time needed to resolve claims, including hiring an attorney, filing or threatening a lawsuit, and negotiating with the insurance company.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card ftdd-pi-chart\"><figure class=\"ftdd-pi-fig\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/pi/resolution-time.webp\" alt=\"Effect of Outcome on Resolution Time: received payout 10mo, received nothing 6.8mo\" width=\"271\" height=\"88\"></figure></div></div>\n<h2 class=\"ftdd-pi-h\">When a Car Accident Case Goes to Trial</h2>\n<p>The vast majority of all car accident insurance claims are resolved before any lawsuit is filed. And of the car accident lawsuits that do get filed, most of those cases are resolved by settlement agreement before a trial takes place.</p>\n<p>But it's also true that not all car accident cases can be settled. Perhaps the parties can’t agree on who caused the accident. Perhaps the parties can agree that the plaintiff was injured, but they can’t come to an agreement on the amount of compensation that should be paid for those injuries.</p>\n<p>If your car accident case cannot be resolved by a settlement, then you may be wondering what happens if your case goes to trial. The rules governing trials vary from state to state, but there are some concepts and procedures for trials that are common to most states, and we'll look at those in the sections that follow.</p>\n<h3>Opening Statements</h3>\n<p>Once the jury is selected, the parties then make opening statements. The plaintiff’s attorney usually goes first, because the plaintiff has the burden of proving all of the allegations in the case. The opening statement is the opportunity for each party’s attorney to set the stage for the jury and lay out their side of the case -- what they will prove or refute. In most states, opening statements usually last about fifteen to twenty minutes.</p>"},{"id":"reading-7","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<h3>The Plaintiff’s Presentation of Evidence</h3>\n<p>Following the opening statements, the plaintiff’s attorney presents the plaintiff’s case. Again, the plaintiff’s side goes first in presenting the evidence because the plaintiff has the \"burden of proof.\" The attorney presents evidence on the issues by calling witnesses.</p>\n<p>For example, to establish how the car accident occurred, the plaintiff’s attorney would probably call the plaintiff to testify about his or her observations just before and during the crash, and at the scene shortly afterward. The attorney may also call any bystanders or other car accident witnesses.</p>\n<p>A similar pattern is followed in presenting evidence on other issues in the case, though the particular witnesses might not be the same.</p>\n<p>For example, to show the jury evidence of the plaintiff’s injuries in the car accident, the plaintiff’s attorney might ask questions directly to the plaintiff regarding the injuries suffered. Following that, the plaintiff’s attorney might call as a witness the plaintiff’s doctor. Questions posed to the doctor might address issues concerning the medical treatment that was required following the car accident, and the plaintiff’s prognosis for a full recovery.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>The Defendant’s Presentation of Evidence</h3>\n<p>Once the plaintiff’s attorney has presented to the jury all of the witnesses the attorney believes necessary to prove the plaintiff’s side of the case, the plaintiff then “rests” the case. Doing so signifies to the judge that it is the defendant’s turn to present evidence.</p>\n<p>The defendant’s presentation of evidence follows the same format as that for the plaintiff. The defendant’s attorney calls witnesses to testify to the jury on the issues raised by the case. Just as in the plaintiff’s case, the testimony of those witnesses called by the defendant’s attorney typically supports the claims and defenses of the side calling the witnesses.</p>\n<p>For example, the defendant’s attorney might call a witness who saw the car accident and who contradicts the plaintiff’s version of the events. On the issue of injuries, the defendant might present another of the plaintiff's treating doctors who has an opinion different than the doctor who was called as a witness by the plaintiff’s attorney.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>Closing Arguments</h3>\n<p>Following the evidence, the attorney for each side gives a closing argument. While the opening statement at the beginning of the trial addresses what each attorney expects the evidence will show, in a closing argument each attorney talks to the jury about the evidence that was actually presented. The closing argument is each attorney’s opportunity to persuade the jury to draw certain conclusions from the evidence, and then render a verdict in favor of a particular party.</p>\n</div></div>\n<h3>Jury Deliberation</h3>\n<p>Following the closing arguments, the jury proceeds to a room apart from the courtroom where it then deliberates on the evidence and eventually reaches a verdict. Jury deliberations in all states are confidential, and neither the parties nor the judge observe the deliberations. Most juries reach a verdict in a car accident case within several hours, though there is no set time limit. Sometimes jury deliberations can last for days.</p>\n<h3>The Jury Reaches a Verdict</h3>\n<p>Once the jury reaches a verdict, it notifies the judge that the deliberations have concluded. The judge then brings the jury back into the courtroom where the verdict is read to the parties and made a part of the official record of the court.</p>\n<p>Jury trials in car accident typically last only a few days from the time jury selection begins until a verdict is reached. However, there is no set rule. The length of a trial largely varies with the complexity of the case and with the local court procedures applicable in your state.</p>"},{"id":"reading-8","h":"Reading Task: Personal Injury","html":"<h2 class=\"ftdd-pi-h\">Time Limits for a Personal Injury Lawsuit: What is the Statute of Limitations</h2>\n<p>If you think you might have a valid personal injury case after any kind of accident, it's crucial to pay attention to the statute of limitations, which is a state law that sets a strict time limit on your right to file a personal injury lawsuit.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pi-row ftdd-pi-pair ftdd-pi-n2\"><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>How Does the Statute of Limitations Work?</h3>\n<p>All states have passed statutes of limitations, which set strict deadlines for the filing of different kinds of lawsuits in the state's civil court system. Most states have a statute of limitations that specifically applies to personal injury cases (or to lawsuits alleging negligence). Whatever statute of limitations applies to your potential case, if the deadline has passed and you try to file a lawsuit anyway, your case will almost certainly be dismissed. There are exceptions that could effectively extend the filing deadline, but they're fairly rare.</p>\n<p>In a personal injury case, the statute of limitations usually begins running on the day you were injured. For example, in a car accident case, it's the date on which the crash occurred.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ftdd-pi-card\">\n<h3>The Standard Statute of Limitations in Personal Injury Cases</h3>\n<p>The statute of limitations in personal injury cases ranges from as short as one year to as long as six years, depending on the state. For details on the law where you live, check the statute of limitations in your state.</p>\n</div></div>\n<h3>The \"Discovery Rule\" Exception to the Statute of Limitations</h3>\n<p>Most states have some form of a \"discovery rule\" exception to the standard statute of limitations deadline in an injury case. In general, the discovery rule extends the filing deadline in situations where, until after the original statute of limitations deadline passed, the injured person did not know (and had no reasonable basis for knowing) that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>they suffered an injury, and/or</li>\n<li>that the potential defendant’s actions may have caused the injury</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This situation is not as uncommon as you might think.</p>\n<p>Example Of The Discovery Rule: Let’s say your state has a two-year statute of limitations for personal injury cases, but that your state has a discovery rule that says that the statute of limitations does not begin running in a personal injury case until the date the plaintiff: 1) knew or had sufficient notice that he/she was injured; and 2) knew or had sufficient notice of the cause of the harm.</p>\n<p>Let’s say you were exposed to asbestos in the insulation in the pipes in your basement, and, as a result, 20 years later, you developed mesothelioma, a form of lung cancer that only comes from asbestos exposure. Your doctor asks you if you have any asbestos in the house. Testing reveals that the pipes in your basement have asbestos insulation, and that the insulation has been flaking off the entire time you've been living in the house.</p>\n<p>The statute of limitations deadline has probably passed (though your lawyer might argue that ongoing exposure equals an ongoing injury), so perhaps the only way you can file a personal injury lawsuit over your asbestos exposure would be through reliance on the discovery rule. So your argument would be that the statute of limitations \"clock\" didn't begin running until the day your doctor told you that your lung cancer was due to asbestos exposure.</p>\n<h3>Other Ways to Extend the Standard Deadline</h3>\n<p>In most states, there are several other methods by which the statute of limitations can be extended. For example, if the defendant left the state for any period of time after causing the accident that led to your injury, in most states, the statute of limitations \"clock\" will pause. So, if the statute of limitations time window for filing a personal injury lawsuit is three years, and the defendant was outside the state for a year after the accident, the statute of limitations in your case would be extended by another year.</p>\n<p>Special lawsuit-filing rules also might apply if the plaintiff is a minor (i.e., under age 18), disabled, or mentally ill or insane.</p>"},{"id":"pm","h":"Installation of SA (Smart Advocate) Plug-ins","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-sa-step\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<h3>How to install the Smart Advocate/SA plug-ins:</h3>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-pair ftdd-sa-pair-first\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-text\">\n<p>1. Install the SA Document Handler/Launcher. Unzip its folder first, then right-click on the zipped file and select \"Extract Here.\" Proceed with the installation.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-file\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-00.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-00.png?v=3x\" alt=\"SADocumentHandler_2023\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-01.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-01.png?v=3x\" alt=\"SADocumentHandler_2023.rar\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n<p class=\"ftdd-sa-link\">Link: <a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"How to install the Smart Advocate/SA plug-ins\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19eFGdoQNXJo2iE46M2G8s2bMJNEIeO8k/view?usp=sharing\">SA Document Handler/Launcher</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-side\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n1\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-02.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-02.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 1\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>1</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n2\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-03.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-03.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 2\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>2</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-04.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-04.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 3\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>3</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n2\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-05.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-05.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 4\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>4</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-06.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-06.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 5\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>5</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-step\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<p>2. For Windows Users, access the link and download the 2nd hyperlink to install Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook plugins on your desktop. Follow steps 2-7 as indicated below the list of hyperlinks on this page:</p>\n<p class=\"url-list\"><a href=\"https://smartadvocate.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KB/pages/71237633/Workstation+Configuration+SaaS+SmartAdvocate+Cloud+Links\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://smartadvocate.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KB/pages/71237633/Workstation+Configuration+SaaS+SmartAdvocate+Cloud+Links</a></p>\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n2\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-07.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-07.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 7\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-08.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-08.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 8\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<p>For Mac Users, access the link and download plugin on your desktop. Follow the steps indicated below the link on this page:</p>\n<p class=\"url-list\"><a href=\"https://smartadvocate.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KB/pages/876020096/Document+Handler+Mac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://smartadvocate.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KB/pages/876020096/Document+Handler+Mac</a></p>\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n2\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-09.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-09.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 9\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-10.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-10.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 10\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-step\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-pair ftdd-sa-pair-wide\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-text\">\n<p>3. Once you have downloaded the Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook plugins, double-click the \"Set Up\" application to install.</p>\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n1\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-11.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-11.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 11\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-side\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-sa-note\"><b>Note: This process may take a little longer to complete the download and installation.</b></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n3\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-12.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-12.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 3\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>3</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-13.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-13.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 4\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>4</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-14.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-14.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 5\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>5</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n2\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-15.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-15.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 6\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>6</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-16.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-16.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 7\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>7</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-step\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<p>4. Lastly, double click the Registry to install.</p>\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n3\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-17.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-17.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 1\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>1</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-18.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-18.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 2\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>2</figcaption></figure>\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-19.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-19.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Screenshot 3\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>3</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-unit\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-pair\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-text\">\n<p><b>Just a heads-up, for the SA plug-ins, for now, there is no way for us to check whether they have successfully installed. We will only know if the installation was successful when we start using the firm’s CMS (SA) which is scheduled for around the 8th or 9th of your classroom training.</b></p>\n<p><b>As long as you have this in your list of installed apps then you're good for now.</b></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-side\">\n<div class=\"shots ftdd-sa-strip ftdd-sa-n1\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-20.png?v=3x\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/sa-20.png?v=3x\" alt=\"Installed apps: SADocumentHandler_2023 and WordSADocumentMergeAddIn\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-step\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-pair ftdd-sa-pair-help\">\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-text\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-sa-help\">For those who still have issues installing Nitro Pro despite carefully following the correct process, you may seek technical assistance from Sanders. For the SA plugins issue, you may reach out to Ivan. Message them at 8AM PST.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-side\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-sa-banner\">Here are the Discord IDs of Sanders and Ivan. Please be reminded once again that their shift starts at 8:00 AM PST.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-sa-contacts\">\n  <div><div class=\"shots\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/discord-sanders.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/discord-sanders.png\" alt=\"Sanders on Discord\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div><p><b>Sanders: sndrrsss9920</b></p></div>\n  <div><div class=\"shots\">\n  <figure><a href=\"/ft/day1/img/discord-ivan.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day1/img/discord-ivan.png\" alt=\"Ivan on Discord\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure>\n</div><p><b>Ivan: kuchiq</b></p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"2":{"day":2,"title":"VA Essentials","heading":"DAY 2 VA Essentials","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Buffer Time","html":"<p>Carryover period for completing any pending Day 1 tasks.</p>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"Common Terms Used & Auto Liability Insurance","of":"s2","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-nolearn\" hidden></div>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Common Terms Used\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eErVAp_HkPPCnpQNJ63S3icIWMCbHi_D/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eErVAp_HkPPCnpQNJ63S3icIWMCbHi_D/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-tiles\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ftdd-tile k-doc\" onclick=\"window.FTDayDecks && FTDayDecks.toAssess(2, '14sz5f3HTQKmryc7Upvlc6qua008rPnmw', '.ftdd-embed-crop', 'Common Terms Used: the reference sheet')\"><span class=\"ftdd-tile-ic\">📄</span><span class=\"ftdd-tile-t\"><b>Common Terms Used – Assessment</b><small>Open it on ✍️ Knowledge Check →</small></span></button></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pgbreak\"></div>\n<p>You may also go to this link for reference: </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-crop=\"1272\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Common Terms Used: the reference sheet\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tmV26rq_1z1mpq1C5hUweLytfyJUtkai/edit?usp=drive_link&amp;amp;amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;amp;sd=true\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tmV26rq_1z1mpq1C5hUweLytfyJUtkai/edit?usp=drive_link&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</a></p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pgbreak\"></div>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"How Auto Liability Insurance Works\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1K9AXO0XZJjGFXHPugLAbjeVgcC3fIZuE/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1K9AXO0XZJjGFXHPugLAbjeVgcC3fIZuE/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-tiles\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ftdd-tile k-doc\" onclick=\"window.FTDayDecks && FTDayDecks.toAssess(2, '11K7q6M8-mbtOU9OYA6wGe-vAKU6HKq6C', '.ftdd-embed-crop', 'Common Terms Used: the reference sheet')\"><span class=\"ftdd-tile-ic\">📄</span><span class=\"ftdd-tile-t\"><b>Auto Liability Insurance – Assessment</b><small>Open it on ✍️ Knowledge Check →</small></span></button></div>\n<p>Update items #5–7 in your <a href=\"#/monitoring\" onclick=\"goto('monitoring'); return false;\">📒 Monitoring Sheet</a>.</p>\n"},{"id":"s2b","h":"Common Terms Used & Auto Liability Insurance: Assessments","of":"s2","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"2:s2-1\"></div>\n<p>      📌</p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span><b>AS YOUR HOMEWORK</b>, which is intended to evaluate your understanding of the common terms frequently used during training and actual tasks, as well as your basic grasp of key auto insurance concepts relevant to future topics like claim creation and coverage review — kindly accomplish the <b>Common Terms Used – Assessment</b> and the <b>Auto Liability Insurance – Assessment</b>: each follows its video on the slide before, and both are on ✍️ Knowledge Check.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>While waiting for your teammates to complete their tasks, please read through the articles below on Personal Injury. Thanks.    </span></p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"2:s2-2\"></div>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Personal Injury reading 1\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZOVrwOTPEz9WuwDRbBsBCNuHqf8wb8h4/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZOVrwOTPEz9WuwDRbBsBCNuHqf8wb8h4/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Personal Injury reading 2\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ni4Yg-dublrci2drQhlMVaqxo53xtfP1/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ni4Yg-dublrci2drQhlMVaqxo53xtfP1/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s3","h":"AM: Classroom Discussion on Law Firm Communication","of":"s3","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">📘 <b>Today’s lesson deck</b> opens from <b>▶ Start Training</b> on 📚 Dashboard, or the 📘 lesson button above — it is not on this slide.</div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"2:s3-3\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">✍️ <b>Today’s Process Questions</b> are answered in the day’s Knowledge Check, after the day’s activities.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"FTDayDecks.toKC(FTDayDecks.dayLesson())\">✍️ Knowledge Check →</button></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s3b","h":"Escalation Handling Exercise","of":"s3","html":"<p><b>Escalation Handling Exercise</b></p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGuqWaTQDM\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Canva\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGuqWaTQDM/4WhISjBbgtrQoPfgGYoOyQ/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGuqWaTQDM\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGuqWaTQDM/4WhISjBbgtrQoPfgGYoOyQ/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s4","h":"HOMEWORK: Softphones and PPTs on Documents & Spreadsheets, Keyboard Shortcuts, and Shadowing Etiquette","html":"<p>📌To be accomplished outside training hours. 📌</p>\n<p><b>Topic: Softphones</b></p>\n<p>Task 1 – Please follow this link to view the instructional video on Softphones. Watch ONE SAMPLE type only from the video for your takeaways on your monitoring sheet. You can continue watching it during your idle time. The purpose of this video is to provide a reference in case you learn in the future which specific softphone your client will use. You can then revisit this video for your reference. </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Softphones: the instructional video\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15aa9GSp3DtOFCG2nQD4CgDPsljA1usQ2/view\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/15aa9GSp3DtOFCG2nQD4CgDPsljA1usQ2/view</a> </p>\n<p><b>Topic: Documents &amp; Spreadsheets, Keyboard Shortcuts, and Shadowing Etiquette</b></p>\n<p>Task 2 – Please review the following PPT materials and pay close attention to the information presented in each slide.</p>\n<p><b>The handouts (2026 version)</b></p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-embed ftdd-embed-folder\"><iframe src=\"https://drive.google.com/embeddedfolderview?id=1-uB07Lu7nPeRpdDwOzvAKFMjZbXKQW-r#grid\" title=\"The handouts (2026 version)\" loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n<p>Task 3 - Update items #8-9 in your monitoring sheet.</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"3":{"day":3,"title":"Reception Training","heading":"DAY 3 Reception Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"Checking of Assignments & the Discussion Deck: PI Workflow, Reception Training and Call Listening","of":"s1","html":"<p>Your trainer checks the two assessments you uploaded to your Assessments/Activities subfolder in the last session, with feedback, item clarifications and enrichment.</p>\n<p>Common Terms Used – Assessment</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Common Terms Used – Assessment\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14sz5f3HTQKmryc7Upvlc6qua008rPnmw/edit?usp=drive_link\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/14sz5f3HTQKmryc7Upvlc6qua008rPnmw/edit?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p>Auto Liability Insurance – Assessment</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Auto Liability Insurance – Assessment\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11K7q6M8-mbtOU9OYA6wGe-vAKU6HKq6C/edit?usp=drive_link\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/11K7q6M8-mbtOU9OYA6wGe-vAKU6HKq6C/edit?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"3:s1-1\"></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"3:s1-2\"></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"3:s1-3\"></div>\n<p><b>The Discussion Deck</b></p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGnZtLpFlA\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Discussion Deck\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGnZtLpFlA/0BPHCZmHCpIqY398SUNVXg/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGnZtLpFlA\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGnZtLpFlA/0BPHCZmHCpIqY398SUNVXg/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">✍️ <b>Today’s Process Questions</b> are answered in the day’s Knowledge Check, after the day’s activities.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"FTDayDecks.toKC(FTDayDecks.dayLesson())\">✍️ Knowledge Check →</button></div></div>\n<p><b>Naming convention:</b> PI_Workflow_and_Reception_Training_Process_Questions (VA’s name)</p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"3:s1-4\"></div>\n<p>Sample Call Recordings</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1l8_cBDRXnt-h8QvDZJWaZMO194DWtdSU?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1l8_cBDRXnt-h8QvDZJWaZMO194DWtdSU?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Sample SOP</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zgK-4uKhdJkUvfOkb9A1Jp73C2wu_UOm/edit?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zgK-4uKhdJkUvfOkb9A1Jp73C2wu_UOm/edit?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day3/img/image12.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day3/img/image12.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day3/img/image17.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day3/img/image17.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"Confidentiality & Call Response Exercise","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Confidentiality &amp; Call Response Exercise</b></p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGu11x9AEk\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Canva\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGu11x9AEk/W8BIWHVh_g3lH_wLODdEKw/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGu11x9AEk\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGu11x9AEk/W8BIWHVh_g3lH_wLODdEKw/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n<p>3. Carlos &amp; Oscar’s Reception Recordings are supplementary materials only and are not included in training hours. Trainees may review them during idle or personal time for additional learning.</p>\n<p>In addition, here are additional reception call recordings of VAs Carlos &amp; Oscar for your future reference. Thank you. </p>\n<p>Carlos’ Reception Recordings</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1bP8yBy9WhPgUOnfh-IAvWI4V6UVeYyeI\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1bP8yBy9WhPgUOnfh-IAvWI4V6UVeYyeI</a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1S3L8ecBadvrN_AmGpeQD98mY1148Rvof\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1S3L8ecBadvrN_AmGpeQD98mY1148Rvof</a></p>\n<p>Oscar’s Reception Recordings</p>\n<p>Oscar’s Reception Activity recordings</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1hRO-cnY1nabG8btm1U9OnZxvqYmiwLyn?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1hRO-cnY1nabG8btm1U9OnZxvqYmiwLyn?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ZGr22vm6RW4avTBCn8tCfGexkZMfsavX?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ZGr22vm6RW4avTBCn8tCfGexkZMfsavX?usp=sharing</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s1c","h":"AM: PI Reception Activity: 6 Practice Calls","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Six calls to Harbor &amp; Pine Injury Law (fictional)</b>, a personal injury firm in Tampa, Florida. Each call has a challenge a receptionist meets on the line. Listen to each one (replay it as often as you need) and extract its <b>5 data points</b> into your worksheet.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-points\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-points-h\">📋 The 5 data points of every call</p><ol><li><b>Caller</b>: their name, and who they are (client, potential client, provider, adjuster, family …)</li><li><b>Callback number</b>: with the extension or best time, if given</li><li><b>Verified?</b>: how the VA verified the caller (name, DOB, date of the accident), or why nothing could be shared</li><li><b>Reason for the call</b>: the case and what they need</li><li><b>Action taken</b>: who it went to, and how (message, transfer, callback)</li></ol><p class=\"ftdd-pic-plus\">➕ And the call’s <b>challenge</b>: what made the call hard, and what the VA did about it.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">1</span><span>The Tow Yard</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:18 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔊 Background noise</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag ftdd-pic-who\">👤 Existing client</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">An existing client calls from the side of a busy road, with trucks and horns behind him.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-1.mp3\" title=\"Call 1: The Tow Yard\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">2</span><span>Breaking Up on the Highway</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:54 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">📶 Connection issues</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag ftdd-pic-who\">👤 Potential new client</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">A potential new client calls from her car on the interstate; the line breaks up, then drops.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-2.mp3\" title=\"Call 2: Breaking Up on the Highway\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">3</span><span>Hablo Poquito Inglés</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:12 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🌐 Language barrier</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag ftdd-pic-who\">👤 Existing client</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">A Spanish-speaking client with very little English calls about a letter she received.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-3.mp3\" title=\"Call 3: Hablo Poquito Inglés\"></audio></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">4</span><span>The Speakerphone Echo</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:29 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🎚️ Audio quality: echo and muffled voice</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag ftdd-pic-who\">👤 Medical provider</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">A provider's billing office calls on a speakerphone in a big room: an echo, a faint voice, a lot of numbers.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-4.mp3\" title=\"Call 4: The Speakerphone Echo\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">5</span><span>The Fast-Talking Adjuster</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:10 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔊 Background noise: call centre</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">⏩ Fast speech</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag ftdd-pic-who\">👤 Insurance adjuster</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">A third-party adjuster calls from a loud call centre, talks fast, and pushes for details about the client.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-5.mp3\" title=\"Call 5: The Fast-Talking Adjuster\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">6</span><span>Mom on the Line</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:27 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔊 Background noise: TV and children</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">😟 Upset caller</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔒 Family member not on the file</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-about\">A client's mother calls from a busy house, upset: her son is back in hospital and she wants to know about his case.</p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-6.mp3\" title=\"Call 6: Mom on the Line\"></audio></div></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"3:pi-calls\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-tiles\"><a class=\"ftdd-tile k-doc\" href=\"/handouts/LSH_Day3_PI_Reception_Activity_Worksheet.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span class=\"ftdd-tile-ic\">📝</span><span class=\"ftdd-tile-t\"><b>PI Reception Activity worksheet</b><small>Download the Word file</small></span></a></div>\n<p><b>Naming Convention:</b> PI_Reception_Activity (VA’s first name). Upload the completed worksheet to your Assessment and Activities Folder and work directly from there to finalize it.</p>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"Homework: CRM/CMS Training Videos","html":"<p>Please watch the CRM/CMS training videos and then update item #12 in your Monitoring Sheet. Thank you.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"CRM/CMS Training Video 1\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dIR3Hl7ybLnUtOk9ycyCbpXGnjR3FzMs/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dIR3Hl7ybLnUtOk9ycyCbpXGnjR3FzMs/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"CRM/CMS Training Video 2\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/12HcMi38KO4898qd262UF_z_gB-IzHn0c/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/12HcMi38KO4898qd262UF_z_gB-IzHn0c/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"CRM/CMS Training Video 3\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pa7Smlp9ePfOEq9YNjWfW6mmaJaeRyDo/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pa7Smlp9ePfOEq9YNjWfW6mmaJaeRyDo/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"CRM/CMS Training Video 4\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IiZJ8yq4fo1dQfM8q-2vd3hxxLAn8659/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IiZJ8yq4fo1dQfM8q-2vd3hxxLAn8659/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"CRM/CMS Training Video 5\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HppO3mZWuROS1XZijVmGiX_yDDFhtHgk/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HppO3mZWuROS1XZijVmGiX_yDDFhtHgk/view?usp=drive_link</a> </p>\n<p><b>Note:</b> If not finished during the workshift, you may go back to it later during your idle time.</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"4":{"day":4,"title":"Reception Training","heading":"DAY 4 Reception Training","slides":[{"id":"s2","h":"Training Video Viewing and Mock Call Preparation","of":"s2","html":"<p>For those who have already completed the tasks, please watch these videos on Reception Training to understand the roles and responsibilities of a Receptionist, as well as the necessary attributes required for the role.</p>\n<p><b>Topic: Handling Reception Tasks</b></p>\n<p>Task 1 - Watch this training video with one of our virtual receptionists. Here you would see the VA demonstrating how to handle all sorts of calls and general receptionist tasks.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Reception Training with Julio [1:49:49]\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G5o0O1fTWjUzxrxIBH1ikbbmh4ywFt5C/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G5o0O1fTWjUzxrxIBH1ikbbmh4ywFt5C/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Task 2 - Update items #10 &amp; 11 in your monitoring sheet.</p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"4:s2-1\"></div>\n"},{"id":"s2b","h":"Mock Call Preparation: the Call Simulator, Ring Channel and CMS","of":"s2","html":"<p>Get ready for this afternoon’s one-on-one mock call: practise on the Call Simulator, then take the call on the Ring Channel with the case files in the CMS.</p>\n<p>📞 Practice a caller: the Call Simulator’s Reception line (an AI caller)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Reception+Mock+Calls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Reception+Mock+Calls</a></p>\n<p>☎ The Ring Channel: the training phone your mock call rings on</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT</a></p>\n<p>🗂 The CMS (Case Management System): the case files</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/</a></p>\n<p>☎️ Front Desk Drill in the CMS</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=reception&flow=reception&drill=1&from=standard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=reception&flow=reception&drill=1&from=standard</a></p>\n<p>Step 1 - Open the Call Simulator’s Reception line and put your headset on. Take practice calls from the AI caller as many times as you like: practice calls are not graded.</p>\n<p>Step 2 - Answer within 3 rings and greet with the firm’s name and your name.</p>\n<p>Step 3 - Authenticate before you discuss anything: the caller’s name, date of loss (DOL), date of birth (DOB), claim number and case number.</p>\n<p>Step 4 - Find the file in 🔎 Case lookup (in the CMS, search by the client’s name with Ctrl / Cmd + K; when names match, it asks for the date of the accident and the date of birth).</p>\n<p>Step 5 - Handle the call by the firm’s rules (📘 Rules, 📇 Directory): answer what you may, or use Hold and Transfer to the right person, screening the call and taking notes before you transfer.</p>\n<p>Step 6 - Fill in the 📝 message slip or case note during the call: who called, their role, the callback number and best time, the case and what they need.</p>\n<p>Step 7 - Close with the closing spiel. Then run the Front Desk Drill in the CMS to practise the same flow on the case files.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-link\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">🎧</span><div><b>Link coming: AI Mock Calls Listening</b><p>Recordings of AI mock calls to listen to before your own. Your trainer adds them here.</p></div></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>🎧 Warm-up before your mock call: the PI practice calls</b></p>\n<p>Replay one or two of Day 3’s practice calls. Listen for how the VA verifies the caller, reads numbers back, and handles the noise, the dropped line or the language barrier: you’ll need the same on your own call.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">1</span><span>The Tow Yard</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:18 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔊 Background noise</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-1.mp3\" title=\"Call 1: The Tow Yard\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">2</span><span>Breaking Up on the Highway</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:54 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">📶 Connection issues</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-2.mp3\" title=\"Call 2: Breaking Up on the Highway\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">3</span><span>Hablo Poquito Inglés</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:12 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🌐 Language barrier</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-3.mp3\" title=\"Call 3: Hablo Poquito Inglés\"></audio></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">4</span><span>The Speakerphone Echo</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:29 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🎚️ Poor audio quality</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-4.mp3\" title=\"Call 4: The Speakerphone Echo\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">5</span><span>The Fast-Talking Adjuster</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:10 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">⏩ Background noise and a fast talker</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-5.mp3\" title=\"Call 5: The Fast-Talking Adjuster\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">6</span><span>Mom on the Line</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:27 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔒 Background noise and an unauthorized caller</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-6.mp3\" title=\"Call 6: Mom on the Line\"></audio></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s2c","h":"Instructions for Mock Calls & Metrics","of":"s2","html":"<p><b>How the mock calls run (one-on-one)</b></p>\n<p>Step 1 - While waiting for your turn, keep practising on the Call Simulator’s Reception line.</p>\n<p>Step 2 - Log in to the Ring Channel and stay on standby: your trainer calls each trainee individually.</p>\n<p>Step 3 - Take the call live with your headset on, from the greeting to the closing spiel; your trainer sees your message slip as you fill it in.</p>\n<p>Step 4 - Only hit ✅ Done on the mock call slide after you have completely finished your one-on-one with the trainer.</p>\n<p><b>Reception Mock Calls Metrics</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day4/img/image7.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day4/img/image7.png\" alt=\"Reception Mock Calls Metrics\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p>Each criterion is scored 0–5; your result is the WEIGHTED AVERAGE of the fourteen, which reaches your Scorecard.</p>\n"},{"id":"s3","h":"PM: Reception Mock Calls (One-on-One)","html":"<p>Your one-on-one Reception mock call with the trainer, scored on the Reception Mock Calls Metrics (the slide before).</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"5":{"day":5,"title":"Reception Training","heading":"DAY 5 Reception Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Buffer Time for Reception Mock Calls","html":"<p>Carryover period for completing any pending tasks from the last session. </p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>☎ Reception Mock Calls (One-on-One)</b></p>\n<p>Your one-on-one Reception mock call with the trainer, scored on the Reception Mock Calls Metrics (below).</p>\n<p>If yours is still to do, use this buffer to get ready: practise on the Call Simulator, then take the call on the Ring Channel with the case files in the CMS.</p>\n<p><b>Mock Call Preparation</b></p>\n<p>📞 Practice a caller: the Call Simulator’s Reception line (an AI caller)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Reception+Mock+Calls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Reception+Mock+Calls</a></p>\n<p>☎ The Ring Channel: the training phone your mock call rings on</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT</a></p>\n<p>🗂 The CMS (Case Management System): the case files</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/</a></p>\n<p>☎️ Front Desk Drill in the CMS</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=reception&flow=reception&drill=1&from=standard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=reception&flow=reception&drill=1&from=standard</a></p>\n<p>Step 1 - Open the Call Simulator’s Reception line and put your headset on. Take practice calls from the AI caller as many times as you like: practice calls are not graded.</p>\n<p>Step 2 - Answer within 3 rings and greet with the firm’s name and your name.</p>\n<p>Step 3 - Authenticate before you discuss anything: the caller’s name, date of loss (DOL), date of birth (DOB), claim number and case number.</p>\n<p>Step 4 - Find the file in 🔎 Case lookup (in the CMS, search by the client’s name with Ctrl / Cmd + K; when names match, it asks for the date of the accident and the date of birth).</p>\n<p>Step 5 - Handle the call by the firm’s rules (📘 Rules, 📇 Directory): answer what you may, or use Hold and Transfer to the right person, screening the call and taking notes before you transfer.</p>\n<p>Step 6 - Fill in the 📝 message slip or case note during the call: who called, their role, the callback number and best time, the case and what they need.</p>\n<p>Step 7 - Close with the closing spiel. Then run the Front Desk Drill in the CMS to practise the same flow on the case files.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-link\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">🎧</span><div><b>Link coming: AI Mock Calls Listening</b><p>Recordings of AI mock calls to listen to before your own. Your trainer adds them here.</p></div></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>🎧 Warm-up before your mock call: the PI practice calls</b></p>\n<p>Replay one or two of Day 3’s practice calls. Listen for how the VA verifies the caller, reads numbers back, and handles the noise, the dropped line or the language barrier: you’ll need the same on your own call.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">1</span><span>The Tow Yard</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:18 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔊 Background noise</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-1.mp3\" title=\"Call 1: The Tow Yard\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">2</span><span>Breaking Up on the Highway</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:54 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">📶 Connection issues</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-2.mp3\" title=\"Call 2: Breaking Up on the Highway\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">3</span><span>Hablo Poquito Inglés</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">3:12 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🌐 Language barrier</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-3.mp3\" title=\"Call 3: Hablo Poquito Inglés\"></audio></div></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pic-row\"><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">4</span><span>The Speakerphone Echo</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:29 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🎚️ Poor audio quality</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-4.mp3\" title=\"Call 4: The Speakerphone Echo\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">5</span><span>The Fast-Talking Adjuster</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:10 · VA Rina</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">⏩ Background noise and a fast talker</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-5.mp3\" title=\"Call 5: The Fast-Talking Adjuster\"></audio></div><div class=\"ftdd-pic ftdd-pic-sm\"><p class=\"ftdd-pic-h\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-n\">6</span><span>Mom on the Line</span><span class=\"ftdd-pic-len\">2:27 · VA Paolo</span></p><p class=\"ftdd-pic-tags\"><span class=\"ftdd-pic-tag\">🔒 Background noise and an unauthorized caller</span></p><audio class=\"ftdd-pic-audio\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"/ft/day3/audio/pi-call-6.mp3\" title=\"Call 6: Mom on the Line\"></audio></div></div>\n\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>Instructions for Mock Calls &amp; Metrics</b></p>\n<p><b>How the mock calls run (one-on-one)</b></p>\n<p>Step 1 - While waiting for your turn, keep practising on the Call Simulator’s Reception line.</p>\n<p>Step 2 - Log in to the Ring Channel and stay on standby: your trainer calls each trainee individually.</p>\n<p>Step 3 - Take the call live with your headset on, from the greeting to the closing spiel; your trainer sees your message slip as you fill it in.</p>\n<p>Step 4 - Only hit ✅ Done on the mock call slide after you have completely finished your one-on-one with the trainer.</p>\n<p><b>Reception Mock Calls Metrics</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day4/img/image7.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day4/img/image7.png\" alt=\"Reception Mock Calls Metrics\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p>Each criterion is scored 0–5; your result is the WEIGHTED AVERAGE of the fourteen, which reaches your Scorecard.</p>\n"},{"id":"s3","h":"Attorney Calendar Management Activity","of":"s3","read":true,"html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"5:s3-1\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-card4\"><p class=\"ftdd-card4-h\">📝 1. The activity</p><p>Please answer the Attorney Calendar Management Activity. Make sure to follow the instructions carefully, and don’t forget to signify done (✅ Done, at the end of the activity’s slides) as soon as you finish. Thanks.</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Instructions</h3>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span>Manage the calendar of an attorney by reviewing and scheduling the provided appointments.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>Review the given appointment details carefully.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">3.</span><span>Use your work Google Calendar for this, treating it as your attorney’s official calendar to plot all appointments.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">4.</span><span>Apply time-blocking and color-coding for clarity:</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#0B8043\"></span></span><span><b>Green</b> – Client Meetings</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#039BE5\"></span></span><span><b>Blue</b> – Internal Meetings</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#D50000\"></span></span><span><b>Red</b> – Court-Related Tasks</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#8E24AA\"></span></span><span><b>Purple</b> – External Events</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#F6BF26\"></span></span><span><b>Yellow</b> – Internal Tasks</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#F4511E\"></span></span><span><b>Orange</b> – Personal Wellness</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"><span class=\"ftdd-sw\" style=\"background:#E67C73\"></span></span><span><b>Pink</b> – Personal Events</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">5.</span><span>Add reminders with appropriate notes for each appointment to ensure all details are covered</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">6.</span><span>For travel blocks reminders, set a practical or reasonable reminder time for your attorney that ensures they have sufficient notice to prepare and depart without rushing, allowing enough buffer to account for traffic, last-minute preparations, and the required early arrival time at the airport or point of departure. (Need to ask Mitch’s preferences)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">7.</span><span>Review the calendar to ensure there are no conflicts, such as overlapping appointments or insufficient time buffers between events.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">8.</span><span>For the location, if it does not provide the exact address, just manually input the location indicated in the activity item. For Travel Blocks, ensure the location is specific, including both the departure point and the destination.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\"></span><span>e.g., John F. Kennedy International Airport → LAX</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">9.</span><span>Add Guests’ email addresses (if applicable):</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Martin Anthony</b> - martin@legalsupporthelp.com</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Michelle Velarde</b> - michelle.velarde@legalsupporthelp.com</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>John Michael Dela Cruz</b> - john.delacruz@legalsupporthelp.com</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Lei Lee Abut</b> - team-litigation@legalsupporthelp.com</span></p>\n<h3>Activity Items</h3>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>1. Client Meeting</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 06, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10:00 AM – 11:00 AM PST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Conference Room B</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Client consultation for Alyssa Lynn Arehart regarding a car accident case. Set a reminder for 15 minutes before the meeting (notification). Ensure all case documents are accessible during the meeting.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Guests:</b> Martin Anthony &amp; Michelle Velarde</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>2. Team Meeting</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 07, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 3:00 PM – 4:00 PM MST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Google Meet</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Weekly team check-in. Set a reminder for 30 minutes before the meeting (email).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Guests:</b> Martin Anthony, Michelle Velarde, John Michael Dela Cruz, and Lei Lee Abut</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>3. Deposition Meeting</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 08, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 11:00 AM – 1:00 PM EST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Attorney’s Office (or Zoom for remote attendees: zoom.us/deposition-meeting-02-04-25)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Deposition preparation with another attorney. Set a reminder 1 day before (email).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Guests:</b> Martin Anthony &amp; Michelle Velarde</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>4. Gym Session</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 08, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 6:30 AM – 7:30 AM EST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Downtown Seattle Fitness Center</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Morning workout. Set a 10-minute reminder before (notification).</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>5. Doctor’s Appointment</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 09, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 9:00 AM – 10:00 AM PST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Central Medical Clinic</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Routine check-up. Set a 1-day reminder to prepare any necessary documents or insurance details (email).</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>6. Court Appearance</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 10, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 9:00 AM – 12:00 PM PST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Washington County Court</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Attorney has a scheduled court hearing. Set a reminder for 30 minutes before the hearing (notification).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Travel Blocks:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>8:00 AM – 9:00 AM for travel to court.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>12:00 PM – 1:00 PM for return travel.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>7. Recorded Statement Meeting</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 10, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 4:00 PM – 5:00 PM CST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Google Meet</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Recorded statement meeting with an insurance adjuster regarding a premises liability case. Set a reminder 15 minutes before (notification).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Guests:</b> Martin Anthony, Michelle Velarde, John Michael Dela Cruz, and Lei Lee Abut</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>8. Networking Dinner Event</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 13, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 6:00 PM – 8:00 PM PST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> The Ritz-Carlton, San Francisco (600 Stockton St, San Francisco, CA 94108)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Attorney attending a networking dinner with potential clients.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Travel Schedule for the Out-of-State Event:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">➢</span><span><b>Travel to San Francisco:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 13, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Time:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>8:30 AM – 9:00 AM: Transportation to Seattle Airport (SEA).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>9:00 AM – 12:00 PM: Flight from Seattle (SEA) to San Francisco (SFO).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Note:</b> Confirm flight details, check in luggage, bring travel documents, bring business cards ,and prepare attire for the event. Set a 1-day reminder before (email).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">➢</span><span><b>Networking Event:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Time:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>6:00 PM – 8:00 PM: Attend the event.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>Arrival: Block 5:45 PM – 6:00 PM for early arrival.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Note:</b> Bring business cards and prepare a short personal introduction. Set a 30-minute reminder before (notification).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">➢</span><span><b>Overnight Stay:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Details:</b> Attorney will stay overnight in San Francisco.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Preparation:</b> Confirm hotel booking and plan transportation after the event.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:1\"><span class=\"lbl\">➢</span><span><b>Return Travel to Seattle:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 14, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Time:</b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>8:00 AM – 8:30 AM: Check out of the hotel and travel to the airport.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:3\"><span class=\"lbl\">-</span><span>10:00 AM – 1:00 PM: Flight from San Francisco (SFO) to Seattle (SEA).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:2\"><span class=\"lbl\">▪</span><span><b>Reminder:</b> 1 day before (email): Confirm hotel check-out and transportation to the airport.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>9. Document Review Session</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 15, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 1:30 PM – 3:00 PM CST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Attorney’s Office</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Allocate time for the attorney to review a high-priority case file. Set a 30-minute reminder before (notification).</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-cal-item\">\n<p class=\"ftdd-cal-h\"><b>10. Family Dinner</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Date:</b> July 15, 2026</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time:</b> 7:00 PM – 9:00 PM MST</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Location:</b> Home</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Details:</b> Dinner with family.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Reminder:</b> 1 hour before (notification): Pick up groceries on the way home.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-calsim\" data-calsim-activity=\"5:s3\"><a class=\"btn btn-navy\" href=\"#/calsim/attorney-activity\">📅 Do this activity on the Calendar Simulator</a></div>\n"},{"id":"s3b","h":"Attorney Calendar Management Activity: Time Zone, Screenshots & Upload","of":"s3","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"5:s3-2\"></div>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"The Attorney Calendar Management Activity\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VNgbFDn3PgkPwkE6g0PwXYxo-7DmU3MP/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VNgbFDn3PgkPwkE6g0PwXYxo-7DmU3MP/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>\n<p>Samples</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Samples\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1lLquhtY5XQd85X5IEXJcRCkpV39UA8wW?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1lLquhtY5XQd85X5IEXJcRCkpV39UA8wW?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-card4\"><p class=\"ftdd-card4-h\">🕒 2. Set the time zone</p><p>REMINDER! Set the appropriate time zone for each activity item. BEFORE saving each appointment, make sure to take a screenshot to capture the correct time zone, as shown in the sample below.</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-gcal\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sample: the event editor, Recorded Statement Meeting, Feb 6, 2025, 2:00pm to 3:00pm, time zone (GMT-05:00) Central Time - Chicago\"><div class=\"ftdd-gcal-top\"><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-x\">✕</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-title\">Recorded Statement Meeting</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-save\">Save</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-more\">More actions ▾</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-gcal-row\"><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-f\">Feb 6, 2025</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-f\">2:00pm</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-to\">to</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-f\">3:00pm</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-f\">Feb 6, 2025</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-f ftdd-gcal-tz\">(GMT-05:00) Central Time - Chicago</span><span class=\"ftdd-gcal-link\">Time zone</span></div></div>\n<p class=\"ftdd-gcal-cap\">The time zone, boxed in red, shows in every screenshot: set it before you save.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-card4\"><p class=\"ftdd-card4-h\">📸 3. The whole calendar</p><p>When taking a screenshot of the entire calendar, untick the LSH calendar (the one in the orange box), then take a screenshot. Just re-enable it afterward.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-card4\"><p class=\"ftdd-card4-h\">📤 4. Upload your 19 screenshots</p><p>You should have a total of 19 screenshots uploaded to your subfolder in the exact sequence shown in the sample screenshot. Thank you.</p>\n<ol class=\"ftdd-seq\"><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">1</span><span>1. Client Meeting</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">2</span><span>2. Team Meeting</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">3</span><span>3. Deposition Meeting</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">4</span><span>4. Gym Session</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">5</span><span>5. Doctor’s Appointment</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">6</span><span>6.1 Court Appearance</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">7</span><span>6.2 Court Appearance: Travel Block for travel to court</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">8</span><span>6.3 Court Appearance: Travel Block for return travel</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">9</span><span>7. Recorded Statement Meeting</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">10</span><span>8.1 Networking Dinner Event</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">11</span><span>8.2 Transportation to Seattle Airport (SEA)</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">12</span><span>8.3 Flight from Seattle (SEA) to San Francisco (SFO)</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">13</span><span>8.4 Event Proper Arrival Block time</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">14</span><span>8.5 Overnight Stay</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">15</span><span>8.6 Return Travel to Seattle: Check out of the hotel and travel to the airport</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">16</span><span>8.7 Return Travel to Seattle: Flight from San Francisco (SFO) to Seattle (SEA)</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">17</span><span>9. Document Review Session</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">18</span><span>10. Family Dinner</span></li><li><span class=\"ftdd-seq-n\">19</span><span>11. Entire Calendar</span></li></ol>\n<div class=\"ftdd-tiles\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ftdd-tile k-interactive\" onclick=\"window.FTCalCheck ? goto('calcheck') : 0\"><span class=\"ftdd-tile-ic\">📅</span><span class=\"ftdd-tile-t\"><b>Calendar Activity Check</b><small>Check each event against the activity before you upload →</small></span></button></div>\n</div>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"6":{"day":6,"title":"Calendar Management Training","heading":"DAY 6 Calendar Management Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"Entire Day: Calendar Management Training Videos","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"6:s1-1\"></div>\n<p>While waiting for your turn to perform, watch the following training videos.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Calendar Management Training: Part 1\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16zrBv2IsafvW0CphoJHf41JgvZZxcGa5/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/16zrBv2IsafvW0CphoJHf41JgvZZxcGa5/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Calendar Management Training: Part 2\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jzhsqPS3pFS_PWK-c9m63wVs--OjtY7o/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jzhsqPS3pFS_PWK-c9m63wVs--OjtY7o/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-embed data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Calendaring 101\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X9l-70zK3G4JjL_JSBTfHiDVcwzjOUmX/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X9l-70zK3G4JjL_JSBTfHiDVcwzjOUmX/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p>Refer to these video links as well for your additional reference. </p>\n<p><b>Scheduling Appointment and Calendar Management </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Scheduling Appointment and Calendar Management\" href=\"https://www.loom.com/share/f35c3a3f805a4833800c893c4c332dbb?sid=f178c63d-eedf-4d2f-8a2e-564ab3eecb8a\">https://www.loom.com/share/f35c3a3f805a4833800c893c4c332dbb?sid=f178c63d-eedf-4d2f-8a2e-564ab3eecb8a</a></p>\n<p><b>Resource for Scheduling Appointment and Calendar Management </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Resource for Scheduling Appointment and Calendar Management\" href=\"https://www.loom.com/share/1e0b0a35cddb41f1b071a99364e3ea88?sid=7ae551c1-23fd-40ca-ac43-eafbb6af9d47\">https://www.loom.com/share/1e0b0a35cddb41f1b071a99364e3ea88?sid=7ae551c1-23fd-40ca-ac43-eafbb6af9d47</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"Entire Day: Calendar Management Mock Calls","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>☎ Mock Calls: how to access the Call Simulator (Ring Channel) and practise on the Calendaring Tool</b></p>\n<p>📞 Practice a caller: the Call Simulator’s Calendar Management line (an AI caller)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Calendar+Management+Mock+Calls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&line=Calendar+Management+Mock+Calls</a></p>\n<p>☎ The Ring Channel: the training phone your mock call rings on</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT</a></p>\n<p>📅 The Calendaring Tool: the Google Calendar Simulator</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/calsim.html?program=FT&track=standard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/calsim.html?program=FT&track=standard</a></p>\n<p>Step 1 - Open the Call Simulator’s Calendar Management line and put your headset on. Take practice calls from the AI caller as often as you like: practice calls are not graded.</p>\n<p>Step 2 - On each call, collect the minimum information: the caller’s name, callback number, date of birth (DOB) and date of loss (DOL).</p>\n<p>Step 3 - Clarify the meeting type (phone, video or in-person) and check the attorney’s rules on the next slide before you offer a time; offer 2–3 alternatives when the requested slot is unavailable.</p>\n<p>Step 4 - Book the appointment on the Calendaring Tool (the Google Calendar Simulator), in the EST time zone, with a specific title (e.g. Client Consultation Meeting – [Client Name]), the notes, and an email reminder a day before.</p>\n<p>Step 5 - Run the Calendaring Tool’s automated review and fix what it flags.</p>\n<p>Step 6 - When it’s your turn, log in to the Ring Channel and stay on standby: your trainer calls you for your one-on-one mock call, scored on the metrics below.</p>\n<p>Reminders:</p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>No need to submit a separate screenshot for your time zone. Just make sure the time zone is visible in the screenshot for each individual appointment upload.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Please follow the proper screenshot numbering shown in the sample so your files remain organized and in sequence within your subfolder.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Make sure to be specific with your event titles. </span></p>\n<p><b>An optimized calendar schedule should follow this structure:</b></p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-ev\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sample event: Client Consultation Meeting - Martin Anthony Gan, Aug 11, 2026, 3:00pm to 4:00pm, (GMT-07:00) Pacific Time - Los Angeles; Google Meet; notification 15 minutes before; Client Meetings calendar; guests Michelle Velarde (organizer) and Martin Anthony Gan; notes in the description\"><div class=\"ftdd-ev-top\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-x\">✕</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-title\">Client Consultation Meeting - <span class=\"ftdd-ev-mark\">Martin Anthony Gan</span></span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-note\">◀ Client’s Name</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-save\">Save</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-when\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Aug 11, 2026</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">3:00pm</span><span>to</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">4:00pm</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Aug 11, 2026</span><span>(GMT-07:00) <span class=\"ftdd-ev-hl\">Pacific Time - Los Angeles</span></span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-link\">Time zone</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-sub\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-box\"></span> All day <span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Does not repeat ▾</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-body\"><div class=\"ftdd-ev-main\"><div class=\"ftdd-ev-tabs\"><b>Event details</b><span>Find a time</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-line\">🎥 <span class=\"ftdd-ev-link\">Join with Google Meet</span> <small>meet.google.com/dyt-voan-kta</small></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-line\">📍 <span class=\"ftdd-ev-f wide\">meet.google.com/dyt-voan-kta</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-line\">🔔 <span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Notification ▾</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">15</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">minutes ▾</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-line\">📅 <span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Michelle Velarde ▾</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-dot\"></span> Client Meetings ▾</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-line\">💼 <span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Busy ▾</span><span class=\"ftdd-ev-f\">Default visibility ▾</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-desc\"><ol><li>Review contract documents prior to the consultation.</li><li>Review the client’s observations, concerns, and instructions regarding the contract.</li><li>Be prepared to discuss the contract and address the client’s questions or concerns during the GMeet consultation.</li></ol></div></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-side\"><div class=\"ftdd-ev-tabs\"><b>Guests</b><span>Suggested times</span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-f wide\">Add guests</div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-guest\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-av\">M</span><span><b>Michelle Velarde</b><small>Organizer</small></span></div><div class=\"ftdd-ev-guest\"><span class=\"ftdd-ev-av\">M</span><span><b>Martin Anthony Gan</b></span></div><p class=\"ftdd-ev-perm\">Guest permissions</p><div><span class=\"ftdd-ev-box\"></span> Modify event</div><div><span class=\"ftdd-ev-box on\">✓</span> Invite others</div><div><span class=\"ftdd-ev-box on\">✓</span> See guest list</div></div></div></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>Calendar Management Mock Calls Metrics</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day6/img/image39.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day6/img/image39.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"Additional Activity: Calendar Management – Mock Call Scenarios","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"6:s2-1\"></div>\n<p>This activity reinforces proper calendar management through mock calls based on common scheduling scenarios handled by the firm. Trainees will respond to simulated inbound calls involving consultations, follow-ups, case meetings, document signings, and urgent attorney requests.</p>\n<p><b>Trainee should:</b></p>\n<ul><li>Accurately schedule appointments by confirming availability, meeting type, duration, and format (phone, video, or in-office).</li><li>Create complete and accurate calendar entries, including appropriate titles and detailed notes reflecting case context and caller demeanor.</li><li>Follow proper call flow and maintain professionalism, adapting to different caller tones (easy, anxious, irritated, impatient, or emotional).</li><li>Set reminders accordingly for the attorney to be reminded.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Please take note of the following guidelines:</b></p>\n<p><b>Minimum Information to Collect from Caller</b> · VA must obtain:</p>\n<ul><li>Name</li><li>Callback Number</li><li>Date of Birth (DOB)</li><li>Date of Loss (DOL)</li></ul>\n<p><b>✅ Scheduling Rules</b></p>\n<ul><li>Identify available slots only</li><li>Avoid lunch, buffer time, and blocked events</li><li>Offer 2–3 alternative times when a requested slot is unavailable</li><li>Clarify meeting type (phone, video, or in-person)</li><li>Plot the appointment in the attorney’s calendar.</li><li>Calendar should be in EST time zone.</li><li>Set an email reminder a day before the event.</li></ul>\n<p><b>📌 Additional Notes</b></p>\n<ul><li>The attorney does not take new client consults after 5:00 PM.</li><li>New client consults are only scheduled on Tuesdays and Thursdays.</li><li>The attorney accepts max 3 new client consults per day.</li><li>Phone consults, status updates, follow up calls, review, regular and urgent meetings, and signing meetings are max 30 minutes.</li><li>Follow-ups are not scheduled during mornings.</li><li>All consultation meetings are phone consults only.</li><li>Phone consults only between 9:30 AM – 3:00 PM; Attorney will call the client - VA must confirm callback number.</li><li>Preparation, strategy, and settlement meetings are max 45 minutes.</li><li>Conference meetings are max 1 hour.</li><li>Attorney requires 15-minute buffer before and after every meeting.</li><li>Same-day bookings require attorney approval.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"6:s2-2\"></div>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"7":{"day":7,"title":"Intake Training","heading":"DAY 7: Intake Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Classroom Discussion on Intake Specialist Training and Call Listening","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">📘 <b>Today’s lesson deck</b> opens from <b>▶ Start Training</b> on 📚 Dashboard, or the 📘 lesson button above — it is not on this slide.</div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"7:s1-1\"></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"7:s1-2\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">✍️ <b>Today’s Process Questions</b> are answered in the day’s Knowledge Check, after the day’s activities.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"FTDayDecks.toKC(FTDayDecks.dayLesson())\">✍️ Knowledge Check →</button></div></div>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Documents to Support the Claim</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=documents%20to%20support%20the%20claim\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=documents%20to%20support%20the%20claim</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Intake Specialist Best Practices</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20best%20practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20best%20practices</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Fee Arrangements: retainer vs. contingency</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20fee%20arrangements\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20fee%20arrangements</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Intake Scenario Exercise","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Intake Scenario Exercise</b></p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGvIBQND5M\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Canva\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvIBQND5M/TSvwREepwfjf9RJnl5DDYQ/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGvIBQND5M\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvIBQND5M/TSvwREepwfjf9RJnl5DDYQ/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n"},{"id":"insurance","h":"AM: Insurance Providers: the carriers you will hear on intake calls","html":"<p>Almost every intake call names an insurance company: the caller's own (<b>1P</b>, first party) and the at-fault party's (<b>3P</b>, third party). These eight carriers come up again and again. Know who they are, so you can recognise them on the call and write them down correctly.</p>\n<h4>Common Insurance Providers</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"ft-table\"><tr><th>Carrier</th><th>What to know</th><th>Claims line</th></tr><tr><td><b>UAIG</b></td><td>United Automobile Insurance Group (Florida). A non-standard auto insurer: drivers other carriers decline or price high. Common on Florida PIP and bodily injury claims.</td><td>On the insurance card or the declarations page</td></tr><tr><td><b>State Farm</b></td><td>The largest US auto insurer (Bloomington, Illinois). Sold through local agents, so callers often name their agent instead of the company.</td><td>1-800-SF-CLAIM (1-800-732-5246)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Progressive</b></td><td>Ohio-based; sells direct and through independent agents. Also writes commercial auto, so you will see it on work-truck and rideshare cases.</td><td>1-800-776-4737</td></tr><tr><td><b>Allstate</b></td><td>Illinois-based; also owns National General, so a caller's card may carry that name instead.</td><td>1-800-ALLSTATE (1-800-255-7828)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Liberty Mutual</b></td><td>Boston-based; also owns Safeco. Writes auto, home and workers' compensation, so it can appear on a work-injury case too.</td><td>1-800-225-2467</td></tr><tr><td><b>Geico</b></td><td>Government Employees Insurance Company, a Berkshire Hathaway company (Maryland). Sells direct, online and by phone.</td><td>1-800-841-3000</td></tr><tr><td><b>Travelers</b></td><td>New York / Hartford. Writes auto, homeowner's and a lot of commercial and business policies: think premises and work-site claims.</td><td>1-800-252-4633</td></tr><tr><td><b>USAA</b></td><td>San Antonio, Texas. Insures only military members, veterans and their families: if the caller or the at-fault driver served, ask.</td><td>1-800-531-8722</td></tr></table></div>\n<p class=\"ftdd-callout\">📌 Always copy the claims number from the client's insurance card, the declarations page or the adjuster's letter. Numbers change, and a regional office or an affiliate may handle the claim.</p>\n<h4>What to collect about insurance on an intake call</h4>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span><b>Whose policy:</b> 1P (the client's own carrier) and 3P (the at-fault party's carrier). Spell the carrier's name exactly as it is on the card.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span><b>Policy number</b> and the <b>named insured</b> (the policy may be in a spouse's or parent's name).</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">3.</span><span><b>Claim number</b>, if a claim is already open, and the <b>adjuster</b>'s name, phone and e-mail.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">4.</span><span><b>Coverage the caller knows of:</b> bodily injury (BI), property damage (PD), PIP / MedPay, UM / UIM. Don't guess: write \"unknown\" and the firm confirms it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">5.</span><span><b>Has the caller given a recorded statement</b> or signed anything from an insurer? If not, they can take the adjuster's details and refer them to the firm.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">6.</span><span><b>Health insurance</b> (and Medicare / Medicaid): it pays treatment now and may have a lien later.</span></p>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Common Insurance Providers</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-common-insurance-providers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-common-insurance-providers</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Opening a 3P claim: what you can and can't share with the insurer</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-3p-claims-what-to-share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-3p-claims-what-to-share</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Insurance Coverage in Personal Injury Claims</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-insurance-coverage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-insurance-coverage</a></p>"},{"id":"forms","h":"AM: Reference: Evidence Checklist, Blank PI Intake Forms & Sample Recordings","html":"<p>Keep these open while you prepare for your intake mock calls. They are your reference for what to ask and which documents support a claim.</p>\n<p>Accident or Injury Claim Documents and Evidence Checklist</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Accident or Injury Claim Documents and Evidence Checklist\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-a8jF7dTZxdoYv4brVSe9GwGrT9MGFnV/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-a8jF7dTZxdoYv4brVSe9GwGrT9MGFnV/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Blank PI Intake Forms [Dog Bite, Medical Malpractice, Premise Liability, Slip &amp; Fall, MVC/MVA]</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Blank PI Intake Forms\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sdpjU_vYPuuvP1U07uHuHYiBcy2uG3kF/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sdpjU_vYPuuvP1U07uHuHYiBcy2uG3kF/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Mock Intake (non-VLF) recording</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Mock Intake (non-VLF) recording\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VMNX0CrUXBtGAf0xkDq8r6sr4NRNDW4S/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VMNX0CrUXBtGAf0xkDq8r6sr4NRNDW4S/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Sample Intake Audio Recordings</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Sample Intake Audio Recordings\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/16o9xsbY9dRIl8-fSBN2B3fNWuEXmo52q?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/16o9xsbY9dRIl8-fSBN2B3fNWuEXmo52q?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Other Intake-Related Documents</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Other Intake-Related Documents\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1UrLBiX0ntxzvyxvRkHBhdTevtoP2jLzX?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1UrLBiX0ntxzvyxvRkHBhdTevtoP2jLzX?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Intake scripts (sample)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829736\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829736</a></p>\n<h4>More sample intake calls</h4>\n<p>Four more practice recordings, each a harder kind of caller. Play one, note how the intake specialist handles it, then open the transcript to check what you heard.</p>\n<div class=\"ftis-calls\"></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"7:s1-3\"></div>"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Scheduled Shadowing (Shadow Buddy or Intake Videos, if unavailable)","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"7:s2-1\"></div>\n<p><b>Example: </b></p>\n<p>Shadowing Intake Specialist Role/ Insurance Communication Role/ Provider Communication Role/ Lien Negotiator Role (Arlene/ Edward/ Vince/ Allesa/ Mario)</p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>@everyone</b> Kindly update this section of your TAM after the session. Thanks.</p>\n<h4>Your TAM: A. Client Communication</h4>\n<p class=\"ftdd-callout\">📌 <b>Where your TAM is:</b> Google Drive → <b>Shared with me</b> → your batch folder (e.g. B073126) → <b>LSH Trainee folder</b> → <b>LSH Task Assessment Manual (TAM) | [Batch]_ [Your Full Name]</b>. It sits beside your Daily Task Tracker and Training Monitoring Sheet, under the Assessments - Activities, Requirements, Spelling Tests and Typing Tests folders.</p>\n<p>To fully understand the duties and responsibilities of a Receptionist and Intake Specialist, you will closely observe someone performing the role. After your shadowing, write your answers to these in this section of your TAM:</p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span>Why are receptionists important?</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>Enumerate the duties and responsibilities of a receptionist.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">3.</span><span>Why are intake specialists important?</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">4.</span><span>Enumerate the duties and responsibilities of an intake specialist.</span></p>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Intake specialist job duties and description</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829735\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829735</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Receptionist Work Guide</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/958866\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/958866</a></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day7/img/image29.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day7/img/image29.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day7/img/image42.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day7/img/image42.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p>Please proceed to watch these intake shadowing videos of Maria Mangaoang. Thank you.   </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Please proceed to watch these intake shadowing videos of Maria Mangaoang. Thank you. https\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SC653puBU7dh4tYjQjXcr8KZ4yhYxsLV/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SC653puBU7dh4tYjQjXcr8KZ4yhYxsLV/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Please proceed to watch these intake shadowing videos of Maria Mangaoang. Thank you. https\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16DavSPhSUGF88UnltYxl932dsZsYkQtY/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/16DavSPhSUGF88UnltYxl932dsZsYkQtY/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Please proceed to watch these intake shadowing videos of Maria Mangaoang. Thank you. https\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_dsswdnznMTWJAykRJkJKMCOoGg-c8pw/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_dsswdnznMTWJAykRJkJKMCOoGg-c8pw/view?usp=drive_link</a>.</p>\n<p><b><i>***Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"8":{"day":8,"title":"Intake Training","heading":"DAY 8: Intake Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Topic 1: Intake Process","of":"s1","html":"<p>After completing your spelling &amp; typing tests, kindly proceed right away to work on these sets of tasks for today’s training session.  Thank you.</p>\n<p><b>Topic 1: Intake Process</b></p>\n<p>Task 1 - Please watch these two videos:</p>\n<p>A. Intake Process Overview</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"A. Intake Process Overview\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wBga2HLLRAzdD_t5s8zgmRVqcKq23TES/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wBga2HLLRAzdD_t5s8zgmRVqcKq23TES/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>B. Saving intake documents and updating fields in the Intake Tab</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"B. Saving intake documents and updating fields in the Intake Tab\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n4cmYMsoKRBm8FxMaeac7-TZkwegVvVW/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n4cmYMsoKRBm8FxMaeac7-TZkwegVvVW/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Task 2 - Update item #14 in your monitoring sheet.</p>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Client Intake Process</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/918345\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/918345</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: First Stage Procedures: Intake</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/procedure-first-stage-intake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/procedure-first-stage-intake</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Saving documents overview</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829738\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/go/829738</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Topic 2: Intake Documents (MVA Cases)","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Topic 2: Intake Documents (MVA Cases)</b></p>\n<p>Task 1 - Watch this video presentation about the Intake Packet and the Intake Documents.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"The Intake Packet and the Intake Documents\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pa2Ezfvxc9bxRP9xq6z3WCWFjlAOJbIz/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pa2Ezfvxc9bxRP9xq6z3WCWFjlAOJbIz/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Before Task 2, choose your Intake Packet and download it. If your trainer assigned you a packet, choose that one.</p>\n<div class=\"ftis-packet\" data-folder=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1JbAieyhJ6XVsRvNXMUUtVfRwY_0KNymT?usp=sharing\"></div>\n<p>Redacted Intake Packets</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Redacted Intake Packets\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1JbAieyhJ6XVsRvNXMUUtVfRwY_0KNymT?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1JbAieyhJ6XVsRvNXMUUtVfRwY_0KNymT?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"8:s1-1\"></div>\n<p>Task 2 - Extract each document from the Intake Packet and rename it properly using the standard naming convention.</p>\n<p>Task 3 - Answer the worksheet for intake documents.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Intake Documents Worksheet\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O1Oxh2vmK7OPFaJjGyjjofZwNZG5vDqJ/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O1Oxh2vmK7OPFaJjGyjjofZwNZG5vDqJ/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</a></p>\n<p>Task 4 - Update #16 (Intake Documents) in your monitoring sheet.</p>\n<p>NOTE: Please create a subfolder under your Assessments/Activities folder and name it after your assigned client. Upload all the extracted intake documents ALONG with the renamed assigned Intake Packet using this naming convention: <b>INTAKE - Packet (VA&#x27;s Name)</b>.  For your completed Intake Worksheet, upload it directly into your Assessments/Activities folder -- NOT inside the subfolder you created for the extracted intake documents.</p>\n<p>Thank you!</p>\n"},{"id":"s1c","h":"AM: Additional Instruction: Naming Convention & Additional Intake Documents","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Additional Instruction:</h4>\n<p>Please don&#x27;t forget to rename each extracted document using our document-naming convention. Refer to the Knowledge Base article OR the most updated naming conventions found in your intake worksheet.</p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Naming Documents and Case Folders</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-06-naming-documents-and-folders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-06-naming-documents-and-folders</a></p>\n<p>Naming convention reference (PDF)</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Naming convention reference (PDF)\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xn7o6kmz7zUc2h6UAj2qIqytr6QoABzM/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xn7o6kmz7zUc2h6UAj2qIqytr6QoABzM/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"8:s1-2\"></div>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: The Intake Packet</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20training%20the%20intake%20packet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=intake%20specialist%20training%20the%20intake%20packet</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Conflict Awareness During Intake</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=conflict%20awareness%20during%20intake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=conflict%20awareness%20during%20intake</a></p>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Sample PI Onboarding Packet: Contract, HIPAA Authorization and Power of Attorney</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-14-sample-onboarding-packet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/doc/lesson-14-sample-onboarding-packet</a></p>\n<p>Here are additional intake documents for your future reference. Kindly check these ADDITIONAL intake documents which are NOT INCLUDED in the training video.</p>\n<p>Additional Intake Documents</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Additional Intake Documents\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fC8iixgMEVV3cDrtU0sFa0N325uVB4mb?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fC8iixgMEVV3cDrtU0sFa0N325uVB4mb?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span>Client Communication Disclosure</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>Signature Certificate</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">3.</span><span>CM Notes</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">4.</span><span>Police Report</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">5.</span><span>TAR/Traffic Accident Report</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">6.</span><span>TAR/Traffic Accident Report with Labels</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">7.</span><span>Traffic Ticket (accomplished)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">8.</span><span>Traffic Ticket with Labels.1</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">9.</span><span>Traffic Ticket with Labels.2</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">10.</span><span>DMV</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">11.</span><span>ISO Claim Search</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">12.</span><span>Insurance vs Lien Disclaimer (newly added)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">13.</span><span>Affidavit of Communication (newly added)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">14.</span><span>Notice and Waiver of Potential Conflict of Interest (latest version of Conflict of Interest Waiver)</span></p>\n<p>Note: Use your PDF Editor to edit PDF documents.</p>\n<p><b>To ensure clarity:</b></p>\n<p>• For your Intake Worksheet task, your reference is the video in Topic 2: Task 1.</p>\n<p>• For your assigned Intake Packet extraction and renaming, refer to Topic 2: Task 2.</p>\n<p>• As for the new documents not covered in the Task 1 video, please refer to the additional documents provided for your reference.</p>\n"},{"id":"s1d","h":"AM: Additional Instruction: Live Session Instructions","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Additional Instruction: Live Session Instructions</h4>\n<p><b>1. Mock Call Execution</b></p>\n<p>• Lead the conversation using standard call handling procedures and protocols.</p>\n<p>• Gather required caller information actively and verify details verbally.</p>\n<p><b>2. CMS Demonstration</b></p>\n<p>• Log in to the CMS with the access your trainer provides at the start of the session.</p>\n<p>• Input caller details directly into the appropriate fields in real time.</p>\n<p>• Share your screen/demonstrate required navigation steps without disrupting the flow of the call.</p>\n<p class=\"ftdd-callout\">📌 <b>Important Notice on CMS Access:</b> Full CMS access is granted only during the live demonstration. The available accounts connect directly to live case files; advance access is restricted to safeguard data integrity and prevent unintended changes. Please rely on the Intake Form link, recordings, and tutorial video for all advance preparation.</p>\n"},{"id":"s1e","h":"AM: Additional Instruction: This Afternoon’s Activities","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Additional Instruction: This Afternoon’s Activities</h4>\n<p>For this afternoon&#x27;s training activities, please be guided by the following <b>additional reminders and instructions:</b></p>\n<p><b>1. Smart Advocate (SA) Demonstration – Saving the Intake Packet and Extracted Documents</b></p>\n<p>You will first demonstrate the process of saving the completed Intake Packet and extracted intake documents <b><i>in VLF&#x27;s CMS --  SA.</i></b></p>\n<p>To prepare, please review the instructional video provided earlier and familiarize yourselves with the steps involved.</p>\n<p>Video: How to Save the Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents in SA</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"How to Save the Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents in SA\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19nLaPeT0PLq2fBSqtC6S2dVYfUYek3pK/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/19nLaPeT0PLq2fBSqtC6S2dVYfUYek3pK/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><b>2. Intake Mock Call Activity – Training Platform (Prototype CMS)</b></p>\n<p>After completing your SA demonstration, you will proceed with the Intake Mock Call Activity <b><i>using the Training Platform.</i></b></p>\n<p>Please review the provided fillable intake forms and call recordings to familiarize yourselves with the required client and incident information and the appropriate intake questions.</p>\n<p>Fillable PI Intake Forms</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Fillable PI Intake Forms\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sdpjU_vYPuuvP1U07uHuHYiBcy2uG3kF/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sdpjU_vYPuuvP1U07uHuHYiBcy2uG3kF/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>You may also explore the Prototype CMS within the Training Platform to become familiar with its fields and navigation.</p>\n<p>Prototype CMS: Intake (a blank intake to fill in as you ask)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=intake&amp;from=standard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lshcasemanagementtraining-trainingcrm.pages.dev/?program=intake&amp;from=standard</a></p>\n<p>During the mock call, you are expected to ask appropriate intake questions, gather all necessary client and incident information, and <b><i>accurately enter the details obtained directly into the corresponding fields in the Prototype CMS, instead of using the fillable intake forms.</i></b></p>\n<p>While waiting for your scheduled turn for the Intake Mock Call Activity, please use your idle time to practice handling intake calls through the Call Simulator.</p>\n<p>Intake Call Simulator (the Intake Line on LSH Ring Channel)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&amp;line=Intake+Mock+Calls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://cm-training-activity.pages.dev/simulators/call.html?program=FT&amp;line=Intake+Mock+Calls</a></p>\n<p>Thank you.</p>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"AM: Demo Tutorial Viewing and Demo Preparation","html":"<p><b><i>Instructional Video_How to Save the Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents in SA</i></b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Instructional Video_How to Save the Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents in SA htt\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19nLaPeT0PLq2fBSqtC6S2dVYfUYek3pK/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/19nLaPeT0PLq2fBSqtC6S2dVYfUYek3pK/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>"},{"id":"s3","h":"PM: Saving the Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents to SA","of":"s3","html":"<p><b>🧑‍🏫 Trainer Facilitated Demo</b></p>\n<p>Your demonstration of saving your assigned Intake Packet and its extracted intake documents in SA (Smart Advocate) is run by your trainer, one trainee at a time. If your shadow buddy confirms a shadowing session, the demo runs at the same time: your trainer pulls you from the session for your turn. Without live shadowing, you watch a recorded shadowing session while you wait.</p>\n<p><b>Before your turn</b></p>\n<ul><li>Every intake document is extracted from your assigned Intake Packet, and every file, the Intake Packet itself included, is renamed under the firm’s naming convention. These are the exact files you upload and report on SA, so this is done before the demo.</li><li>Your task is posted in SA’s Tasks tab: <i>Intake Packet and Intake Documents Saving Tasks</i>, naming the Intake Packets to save.</li><li>SA lets only one user in at a time: your trainer gives you access for your turn, with 10–15 minutes first to explore it.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Additional Reminder</b></p>\n<p>The same process should be repeated for all extracted intake documents until all available files are uploaded and verified.</p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"8:dd-demo\"></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"8:s3-1\"></div>\n<p><b>Saving Intake Packet and Extracted Intake Documents to SA Demo Metrics</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day8/img/image31.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day8/img/image31.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"s3b","h":"PM: Atty. Sandy’s Video: Intake Calling (MVC)","of":"s3","html":"<p><b>Atty. Sandy’s Video: Intake Calling (MVC)</b></p>\n<p>Watch this training video with Atty. Sandy Van on how to handle Intake Calls for MVC cases.</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Atty. Sandy Van: Intake Calls for MVC cases\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KGd9N0hCGdiY79O1uqB6GOe1d4GAayOh/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KGd9N0hCGdiY79O1uqB6GOe1d4GAayOh/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><b><i>***Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"9":{"day":9,"title":"Intake Training","heading":"DAY 9: Intake Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Buffer Time for Intake Demo","html":"<p>Carryover period for completing the Intake demo. Any remaining time in the morning session shall be allocated for intake mock call preparation.</p>"},{"id":"s2","h":"AM: Intake Mock Call Preparation","html":"<p>While you wait for your turn, practise intake calls on the Call Simulator — the Intake Line on ☎ LSH Ring Channel. Take as many practice callers as you like: they are not scored, and the line is the same one your graded call rings on.</p><p>Run through the intake questions in order, enter what you gather straight into the Prototype CMS's fields as you go, and close by confirming the callback number and what happens next.</p><p><b>Intake Mock Calls Metrics</b></p><p><b>After the mock calls:</b> a debrief is scheduled once everyone's calls are done — your trainer runs through the scorecard with you, what went well and what to change before the next one.</p>\n<h4>📚 In the Knowledge Base</h4>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Lead Call Flow & Required Information</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=lead%20call%20flow%20required%20information\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://lsh-knowledge-base.legalsupporthelp.workers.dev/#/search?q=lead%20call%20flow%20required%20information</a></p>"},{"id":"guide","h":"PM: PI Equivalent Transcription Activity: the Sample Guide (Atty. Magdalena)","html":"<p>Before you transcribe the two interview recordings, work through the sample guide: a personal injury consultation between Atty. Magdalena (<b>A</b>, Attorney) and a new client (<b>C</b>, Client) after a rear-end collision. Listen to it, read the A / C transcript, then compare your own notes with the sample minutes made from it. That is the standard your minutes are scored against.</p>\n<div class=\"ftis-consult\"></div>\n<p><b>Transcription Activity Metrics</b></p>"},{"id":"s3","h":"PM: Transcription Activity: Minutes of the Meeting","of":"s3","html":"<h5>3.1. Minutes of the Meeting Transcription Activity: Client-to-Attorney Activity</h5>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"9:s3-1\"></div>\n<p>Transcription - Recording 1 (va’s first name)</p>\n<p>Transcription - Recording 2 (va’s first name)</p>\n<p>Once each transcription is completed, save the file in your Assessments/Activities folder.</p>\n<p>Sample Minutes of the Meeting/Transcription:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Sample Minutes of the Meeting/Transcription: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CAGSbA5_REY8\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CAGSbA5_REY8UqvCAfn2khyDEL4QMR0m/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CAGSbA5_REY8UqvCAfn2khyDEL4QMR0m/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Interview Recording 1:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Interview Recording 1: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N_cSvNZRWaamyBOwtOijyH-MnmOgRaIi/v\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N_cSvNZRWaamyBOwtOijyH-MnmOgRaIi/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N_cSvNZRWaamyBOwtOijyH-MnmOgRaIi/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p>Interview Recording 2:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Interview Recording 2: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lCC6wYca8Pxgqdw2sos-Bo95JdKtUsT5/v\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lCC6wYca8Pxgqdw2sos-Bo95JdKtUsT5/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lCC6wYca8Pxgqdw2sos-Bo95JdKtUsT5/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><b>Listen here: the two interview recordings</b></p>\n<p>Interview Recording 1</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-embed ftdd-embed-rec\"><iframe src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N_cSvNZRWaamyBOwtOijyH-MnmOgRaIi/preview\" title=\"Interview Recording 1\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n<p>Interview Recording 2</p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-embed ftdd-embed-rec\"><iframe src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lCC6wYca8Pxgqdw2sos-Bo95JdKtUsT5/preview\" title=\"Interview Recording 2\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n<p><b>Read here: the Sample Minutes of the Meeting</b></p>\n<div class=\"ftdd-embed\"><iframe src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CAGSbA5_REY8UqvCAfn2khyDEL4QMR0m/preview\" title=\"Sample Minutes of the Meeting\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n"},{"id":"s3b","h":"PM: Intake Mock Calls","of":"s3","html":"<h5>3.2. Mock Calls</h5>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"9:s3-2\"></div>\n<p><b>Intake Mock Calls Metrics</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day9/img/image23.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day9/img/image23.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p><b><i>***Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"10":{"day":10,"title":"Insurance Communication Training","heading":"DAY 10: Insurance Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Classroom Discussion on Insurance Communication Training and Call Listening","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"10:s1-1\"></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"10:s1-2\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">✍️ <b>Today’s Process Questions</b> are answered in the day’s Knowledge Check, after the day’s activities.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"FTDayDecks.toKC(FTDayDecks.dayLesson())\">✍️ Knowledge Check →</button></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Claims Terminology Exercise","of":"s1","html":"<p> Claims Terminology Exercise</p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGvPSukyvs\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Canva\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvPSukyvs/s8w2Yn1YKOv1k1_N-pxDgw/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGvPSukyvs\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvPSukyvs/s8w2Yn1YKOv1k1_N-pxDgw/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s1c","h":"AM: Opening Claims: What to Share & VA Call Recordings","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"10:s1-3\"></div>\n<p><b>Additional Information:</b></p>\n<p>If you’re opening a claim or checking for an existing claim with the 3P&#x27;s insurance, please take note of the following:</p>\n<p><b>Do NOT share the following sensitive information:</b></p>\n<p>Date of Birth (DOB)</p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span>Email Address</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>Social Security Number (SSN)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">3.</span><span>Vehicle Identification Number (VIN)</span></p>\n<p><b>What you CAN share:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">1.</span><span>Client’s Name (First and Last only – no middle name)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">2.</span><span>Vehicle Information (e.g., License Plate Number)</span></p>\n<p><b>To check under the 3P insurance, you may also provide:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Client’s Address (City and State only)</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Phone Number (Give the law firm’s number)</span></p>\n<p><i>Note:</i></p>\n<p>The pieces of information you’re allowed to share are typically available in the police report, something the adjuster would likely already have access to </p>\n<p>Sample Insurance Communication-Related Documents and VA Recordings</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Sample Insurance Communication-Related Documents and VA Recordings https://drive.google.co\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14jCcagQ9mGag2DyRxFPCN-bWds5tl_bU?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14jCcagQ9mGag2DyRxFPCN-bWds5tl_bU?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><b>VA Call Recordings: Opening Claims/Checking For Existing Claims </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-v5NyBlz4dupb3L6aMx4PWRdyx5iAIAr?usp=drive_link, h\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-v5NyBlz4dupb3L6aMx4PWRdyx5iAIAr?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-v5NyBlz4dupb3L6aMx4PWRdyx5iAIAr?usp=drive_link</a>,<a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-v5NyBlz4dupb3L6aMx4PWRdyx5iAIAr?usp=drive_link, h\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15OCezerotGu4tql8gOOxleQYN4uVSWJJ?usp=drive_link\"> https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15OCezerotGu4tql8gOOxleQYN4uVSWJJ?usp=drive_link</a> </p>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Insurance Communication Videos and Articles Review Tasks","html":"<p>For your tasks this afternoon, kindly go over these videos and the job aid or work guide article for additional reference. If you don&#x27;t manage to finish them, you can watch them during your idle time. Thank you. </p>\n<p><b>OPENING CLAIMS &amp; SENDING LOR</b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"OPENING CLAIMS &amp; SENDING LOR https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wN9gMcmp7YVOIjGJLItSWl_4wbFa\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wN9gMcmp7YVOIjGJLItSWl_4wbFarIz4/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wN9gMcmp7YVOIjGJLItSWl_4wbFarIz4/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>\n<p><b>SAMPLE OPENING A CLAIM W/ 3P ZURICH</b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"SAMPLE OPENING A CLAIM W/ 3P ZURICH https://drive.google.com/file/d/1W86a49udA9MqS2v4HuUDA\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1W86a49udA9MqS2v4HuUDAEi6MXMaLBpo/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1W86a49udA9MqS2v4HuUDAEi6MXMaLBpo/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><b>TOOLS OVERVIEW BY CYREL ALEGADO </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"TOOLS OVERVIEW BY CYREL ALEGADO https://drive.google.com/file/d/18FUTlC2dl0blz_MoLLGPoQrwP\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18FUTlC2dl0blz_MoLLGPoQrwP3ysYfrm/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/18FUTlC2dl0blz_MoLLGPoQrwP3ysYfrm/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><b>FAMILIARIZING INTAKE DOCUMENTS </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"FAMILIARIZING INTAKE DOCUMENTS https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KzHQdSRugd53_puQXYWu4moiza\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KzHQdSRugd53_puQXYWu4moizaMeCRz3/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KzHQdSRugd53_puQXYWu4moizaMeCRz3/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><b>OBTAINING COVERAGE INFORMATION</b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"OBTAINING COVERAGE INFORMATION https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LrxtH7zguRVMpcE-6IJbAz366V\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LrxtH7zguRVMpcE-6IJbAz366VyfkW1Y/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LrxtH7zguRVMpcE-6IJbAz366VyfkW1Y/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p>Kindly go over this job aid or work guide article during your idle time for additional reference</p>\n<p><b>HOW TO OPEN A 3P AUTO INSURANCE CLAIM &amp; SENDING LOR  - VLF’s SOP </b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"HOW TO OPEN A 3P AUTO INSURANCE CLAIM &amp; SENDING LOR - VLF’s SOP https://drive.google.com/f\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cBIq48EPE4kUxJXRPGISPhpl61Jsb-gN/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cBIq48EPE4kUxJXRPGISPhpl61Jsb-gN/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"11":{"day":11,"title":"Insurance Communication Training","heading":"DAY 11: Insurance Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Policy Disclosure, Claim & Liability Evaluation","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s1-1\"></div>\n<p>Proceed to the assessment activity designed to evaluate your understanding of key responsibilities as an Insurance Claim Specialist.</p>\n<p><b>Policy Disclosure, Claim &amp; Liability Evaluation</b></p>\n<p>Objective: To assess your ability to accurately review, analyze, interpret, and extract relevant insurance policy information from Dec Pages (Declarations Pages), demonstrate an understanding of insurance coverages, fault, negligence, and liability, and apply this knowledge to the claim-handling process, including identifying the essential information and documentation required to open a claim.</p>\n<p>This evaluation consists of 2 components:</p>\n<p><b>1. Policy Disclosure</b></p>\n<p>-- Reference: Use the <b>zipped file containing the Dec Page</b> as your source material.</p>\n<p><b>2. Claim &amp; Liability Evaluation</b></p>\n<p>-- Complete this component based on your understanding of the concepts and processes covered during training.</p>\n<p><b>Important:</b> Before starting the evaluation, <b>download all required files</b> and make sure you are referring to the correct Dec Page for each Policy Disclosure activity. </p>\n<p>Thank you.</p>\n<p>Assessment Activities</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Assessment Activities https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LX_skojUHS2NbxKMd_lrJvfiXuFZ\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LX_skojUHS2NbxKMd_lrJvfiXuFZI2bD?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LX_skojUHS2NbxKMd_lrJvfiXuFZI2bD?usp=sharing</a><u> </u></p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s1-2\"></div>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: LOR Drafting Activity","of":"s1","read":true,"html":"<p>As soon as you’re done with Activities 1 &amp; 2 of your Claim and Liability Evaluation, please proceed right away to drafting your LORs. </p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day11/img/image26.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day11/img/image26.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s1-3\"></div>\n<h3>Objective</h3>\n<p>The purpose of this activity is to draft a Letter of Representation for both 1P and 3P. Your letter should be accurate, professional, and follow the proper format. Attention to detail is critical for this task, as it reflects your ability to communicate legal matters clearly and effectively.</p>\n<h3>Activity 1: Letter of Representation/LOR Drafting for 1P</h3>\n<p><b>Instructions:</b></p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Use the Template:</b><ul><li>Open the LOR template provided in the training GC.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Input Assigned Case Details:</b><ul><li>Replace all placeholders in the template with accurate information from your assigned case (case notes sent via DM).</li><li>Remove all brackets when replacing placeholders.</li><li>Follow the correct capitalization format used in the placeholders (ALL CAPS vs. regular text).</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Review and Verify:</b><ul><li>Carefully examine the highlighted sections in the letter.</li><li>Not all highlighted items may require changes; however, each must be reviewed for accuracy and relevance based on your case notes.</li><li>Make all necessary edits to ensure the letter accurately reflects the case specifics.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Attention Line:</b><ul><li>If no adjuster is assigned: write \"Attention: Claims Department\".</li><li>If an adjuster is assigned: include the adjuster's name.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Claims to be Opened:</b><ul><li>For this activity, tick all types of claims.</li><li>(Note: In real scenarios, claims to be opened will depend on the client’s available insurance coverage.)</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Letter Date:</b><ul><li>Use the current date as the letter’s date (i.e., the date the letter is drafted).</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Formatting and Grammar:</b><ul><li>Ensure correct spelling, grammar, punctuation, and professional formatting, consistent with formal letter-writing standards.</li><li>Pay close attention to the proper formatting of the recipient’s address section.</li><li>The letter template is firm-specific, there is no need to reformat the body of the letter. Focus only on the highlighted sections.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Saving the File:</b><ul><li>Save your drafted LOR in your assigned Assessment/Activities folder.</li><li>Use this naming convention: <b>INS – 1P Insurance Provider - LOR mm.dd.yyyy (VA's name)</b></li></ul></li>\n</ol>\n"},{"id":"s1b-2","h":"AM: LOR Drafting Activity","of":"s1","read":true,"html":"<h3>Activity 2: Letter of Representation (LOR) Drafting for 3P</h3>\n<p><b>Instructions:</b></p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Use the Template:</b><ul><li>Open the LOR template provided in the training GC.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Input Assigned Case Details:</b><ul><li>Replace all placeholders in the template with accurate information from your assigned case (case notes sent via DM).</li><li>Remove all brackets when replacing placeholders.</li><li>Follow the correct capitalization format used in the placeholders (ALL CAPS vs. regular text).</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Review and Verify:</b><ul><li>Carefully examine the highlighted sections in the letter.</li><li>Not all highlighted items may require changes; however, each must be reviewed for accuracy and relevance based on your case notes.</li><li>Make all necessary edits to ensure the letter accurately reflects the case specifics.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Attention Line:</b><ul><li>If no adjuster is assigned: write \"Attention: Claims Department\".</li><li>If an adjuster is assigned: include the adjuster's name.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Letter Date:</b><ul><li>Use the current date as the letter’s date (i.e., the date the letter is drafted).</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Formatting and Grammar:</b><ul><li>Ensure correct spelling, grammar, punctuation, and professional formatting, consistent with formal letter-writing standards.</li><li>Pay close attention to the proper formatting of the recipient’s address section.</li><li>The letter template is firm-specific, there is no need to reformat the body of the letter. Focus only on the highlighted sections.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Saving the File:</b><ul><li>Save your drafted LOR in your assigned Assessment/Activities folder.</li><li>Use this naming convention: <b>INS – 3P Insurance Provider - LOR with Affidavit mm.dd.yyyy (VA's name)</b></li></ul></li>\n</ol>\n"},{"id":"s1b-3","h":"AM: LOR Drafting Activity: Templates, Case Notes & Reminders","of":"s1","html":"<p>1P LOR Template</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"download all required files\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aRMbhtBTZ3wxDDo5Ww1sERL5frjdNNHw/edit?usp=sharing\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aRMbhtBTZ3wxDDo5Ww1sERL5frjdNNHw/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</a> </p>\n<p>3P LOR Template</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"DAY 11: Insurance Communication Training\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10Nz45QtxH3O6RSBH3A83sl_RpUJ-rF0P/edit?usp=sharing\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/10Nz45QtxH3O6RSBH3A83sl_RpUJ-rF0P/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</a> </p>\n<p>Case Notes</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"DAY 11: Insurance Communication Training\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16pAsNo35SkAMlqwhMQR5wE-xJ5oMZbsK/edit?usp=sharing\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/16pAsNo35SkAMlqwhMQR5wE-xJ5oMZbsK/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=107426275770887856664&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</a></p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s1-4\"></div>\n<p><b>Additional Reminders for Drafting Your LOR:</b></p>\n<p>• Clarification on “F/E”: “F/E” stands for Fax or Email. Refer to your case notes for the available method of sending.</p>\n<p>• In the recipient’s address section, update the line that says “SENT VIA FACSIMILE AND E-MAIL” by keeping only the method you selected (either Facsimile or E-mail) and removing the other.</p>\n<p>• In the “F/E” part, replace it with the actual fax number or email address you’ll be using to send the letter.</p>\n<p> <b>Before saving your LOR in your Assessments folder:</b></p>\n<p>• Review thoroughly for completeness and correctness.</p>\n<p>• Ensure proper formal letter formatting, including:</p>\n<p>        -Correct spacing</p>\n<p>        -Proper layout of the recipient’s address section</p>\n<p>        -Consistent font and alignment</p>\n<p> •  Follow the specific instructions listed in the activity sheet, especially on what must be checked, updated, or edited.</p>\n<p>Lastly, keep in mind that these letters will be sent to insurance companies.</p>\n<p>Make sure your final draft is:</p>\n<p>       •  Clear</p>\n<p>       •  Accurate</p>\n<p>       •  Professionally written</p>\n<p>❗ There should be <b>NO</b> highlighted texts left in your final output. ❗</p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s1-5\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">🧰 <b>Draft your 1P and 3P letters</b> in the platform’s LOR Drafting tool.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"goto('lor')\">🧰 Open the LOR Drafting tool →</button></div></div>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Shadowing","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"11:s2-1\"></div>\n<p><b>Note: </b>If no shadowing buddy is available, recorded shadowing video/s will be provided to trainees instead.</p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>@everyone</b> Kindly update this section of your TAM after the session. Thanks.</p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day11/img/image32.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day11/img/image32.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p><b>Note:</b> To be given in lieu if the shadow buddy is not available for a shadowing.</p>\n<p><b>SHADOWING ASTRED 09/20: INTAKE SUPPORT &amp; PI CLAIMS SPECIALIST ROLES</b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"SHADOWING ASTRED 09/20: INTAKE SUPPORT &amp; PI CLAIMS SPECIALIST ROLES https://drive.google.c\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fbrRvkeisnNF7EfVxCKTGtEodR7MY0A8/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fbrRvkeisnNF7EfVxCKTGtEodR7MY0A8/view?usp=dri</a></p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"12":{"day":12,"title":"Insurance Communication Training","heading":"DAY 12: Insurance Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Tutorial Video: Saving LORs to SA and Sending to 1P & 3P Insurance Companies","of":"s1","html":"<p><b><i>Tutorial Demo Recording on Saving LORs to SA and Sending to 1P &amp; 3P Insurance Companies</i></b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Tutorial Demo Recording on Saving LORs to SA and Sending to 1P &amp; 3P Insurance Companies ht\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zLB0gIWZpMCozH2U3hpw8qmgKtvcjO9W/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zLB0gIWZpMCozH2U3hpw8qmgKtvcjO9W/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Adding 1P and 3P Insurance Information","of":"s1","html":"<p>When creating your process guide for your Saving LORs to SA and Sending to 3P &amp; 1P Ins Companies Demo, please incorporate these additional and updated steps, as they are already available in SA, particularly when entering insurance information for both 1P and 3P. </p>\n<p><b>ADDING 1P and 3P INSURANCE INFORMATION</b> </p>\n<p><b>For BOTH 1P and 3P insurance entries, make sure to complete the following fields:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Policy Number</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Claim Number</span></p>\n<p><b>When adding the 1P insurance information:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>In the <b>Plaintiff Insurance Owner Field</b>, select: <b>Plaintiff&#x27;s Training Acct</b></span></p>\n<p><b>In the Comments section, include the following:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Actual insurance name of the owner</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Assigned adjuster details</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>If no adjuster has been assigned yet, indicate: <b><i>“No adjuster assigned yet.”</i></b></span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Still add all other available insurance information even if no adjuster has been assigned.</span></p>\n<p><b>When adding the 3P insurance information:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>In the <b>Defendant Insurance Owner field</b>, select: <b>OWNER, FAKE</b></span></p>\n<p><b>In the Comments section, include the following:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Actual insurance name of the owner</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Driver’s name, if different from the owner</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Assigned adjuster details</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>If no adjuster has been assigned yet, indicate: “<b><i>No adjuster assigned yet.</i></b>”</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Still add all other available 3P insurance information even if no adjuster has been assigned.</span></p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p>Please take note and include these reminders &amp; updates in your notes/work guide. </p>\n"},{"id":"s1c","h":"AM: Tools & Naming Convention","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Tools:</b></p>\n<p>1. CMS: Smart Advocate</p>\n<p>2. Notepad</p>\n<p>3. Nitro Pro (pdf editing tool)</p>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p><b>Complete Naming Convention: </b></p>\n<p>INS – 1P/3P Insurance Provider - LOR mm.dd.yy (VA&#x27;s name)</p>\n<p><b>Samples:</b></p>\n<p>INS – 1P State Farm – LOR 02.17.2026 (Michelle) </p>\n<p>INS – 3P Geico – LOR with Affidavit 02.17.2026 (Michelle)</p>\n"},{"id":"s1d","h":"Entire Day: Recorded Demonstration - Uploading and Sending 1P & 3P LORs","of":"s1","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"12:s1-1\"></div>\n<h4>Saving LORs to SA and Sending to 1P &amp; 3P Insurance Companies Metrics</h4>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day12/img/image27.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day12/img/image27.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"13":{"day":13,"title":"Provider Communication Training","heading":"DAY 13: Provider Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Buffer Time for LOR Drafting Demo","html":"<p>Carryover period for completing the demo.  </p>"},{"id":"s3","h":"PM: Breakout Session & Document Detectives Exercise","of":"s3","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"13:s3-1\"></div>\n<div class=\"ftdd-pq\">✍️ <b>Today’s Process Questions</b> are answered in the day’s Knowledge Check, after the day’s activities.<div class=\"ftdd-pq-go\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-navy\" onclick=\"FTDayDecks.toKC(FTDayDecks.dayLesson())\">✍️ Knowledge Check →</button></div></div>\n<p><b>Document Detectives Exercise</b></p>\n<div class=\"canva-frame\" id=\"cvDAGvaFyDPHo\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Canva\" src=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvaFyDPHo/DXv2IzUJscIB_JMVcyVUSQ/view?embed\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe></div><div class=\"actions\"><span></span><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn ghost\" type=\"button\" data-fullscreen=\"cvDAGvaFyDPHo\">⛶ Full screen</button><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.canva.com/design/DAGvaFyDPHo/DXv2IzUJscIB_JMVcyVUSQ/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open in Canva ↗</a></div></div>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day13/img/image34.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day13/img/image34.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><figure><a href=\"/ft/day13/img/image30.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day13/img/image30.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"13:s3-2\"></div>\n<p><b>Sample recordings &amp; documents for your reference</b></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"doc\" data-title=\"Sample recordings &amp; documents for your reference https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/17\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/17_v7RMsD93ebLoq9mu7srIqkcxEL-Egk?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/17_v7RMsD93ebLoq9mu7srIqkcxEL-Egk?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"s3b","h":"HOMEWORK: HIPAA Training 101","of":"s3","html":"<p><b>HIPAA Certificate Task</b></p>\n<p>Please watch the HIPAA Training 101 series of short videos and complete all the modules. After completing the entire series, take a screenshot of the final page of the last video, making sure the timestamp is visible, as proof of completion. Once done, please DM the screenshot to Michelle.</p>\n<p>HIPAA Training 101 series</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://compliancy-group.com/free-hipaa-training/hipaa-introduction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://compliancy-group.com/free-hipaa-training/hipaa-introduction/</a> </p>\n<p><b>Naming Convention:  </b>HIPAA Certificate_[Your Name]</p>\n<p>Thank you.  </p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day13/img/image22.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day13/img/image22.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"14":{"day":14,"title":"Provider Communication Training","heading":"DAY 14: Provider Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Tutorial Video - Sending MedLOR (Medical Letter of Representation) and Requesting for Medical Bills & Records","of":"s1","html":"<p>Please proceed to watch the tutorial video and learn how we, here at VLF handle the process of sending MedLOR and requesting medical bills and records. </p>\n<p><b>Topic: Sending MedLOR (Medical Letter of Representation) and Requesting for Medical Bills &amp; Records</b></p>\n<p>Tutorial Video:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Tutorial Video: https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p>NOTE:  While watching the tutorial video, create your own notes or work guide so that you have something to refer to during your recorded demonstration. Additionally, please skip [Time stamp range 58:12-58:45 mins] in the video. Thank you.</p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Notes for Your Work Guide","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Please take note and include these reminders &amp; updates in your notes/work guide. </h4>\n<p><b>Tools:</b></p>\n<p>1. CMS: Smart Advocate</p>\n<p>2. Notepad</p>\n<p>3. Nitro Pro (pdf editing tool)</p>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p><b>Complete Naming Convention: </b></p>\n<p>MED - Lien Holder(Medical Provider) - MedLOR with Unsworn COR and HIPAA mm.dd.yy (va’s first name)</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<p>MED - JML(Lyons Physical Therapy) - MedLOR with Unsworn COR and HIPAA 08.11.22 (John)</p>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p><b>Please add these in your notes. </b></p>\n<p>1. HIPAA Form</p>\n<p>*Validity of Authorization Form - Enter the date when the client signed the form, as indicated below the document </p>\n<p>*Relationship to Patient – Self</p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day14/img/image25.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day14/img/image25.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p>2. In MedLOR </p>\n<p>- tick the appropriate box (for bills &amp; records) as indicated in your request</p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day14/img/image46.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day14/img/image46.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p>3. Naming convention for NPIM (Nevada Personal Injury Management) doctors</p>\n<p>- indicate the name of the doctor</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<p>MED - JML(Fabito Anesthesia Pain Center Dr. Fabito) - MedLOR with Unsworn COR and HIPAA 08.11.22 (John)</p>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p>4. <b>Sending request: E-mail/E-filing</b></p>\n<p>Subject Line:   </p>\n<p>Name of the client - Name of the lien holder(medical provider) - Type of Request</p>\n<p>Jane Doe - JML(Fabito Anesthesia Pain Center Dr. Fabito) - Request for Medical Bills and Records</p>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<p><b>Provider - Nevada Personal Injury Management (NPIM)</b></p>\n<p><b>List of doctors under NPIM</b></p>\n<p>- Dr. Brian Le</p>\n<p>- Dr. Thomas Yee</p>\n<p>- Dr. Daniel Fabito</p>\n<p>- Dr. Anthony Ruggeroli</p>\n<p>- Dr. Quan Haduong</p>\n<p>- Dr. Sudhir Khemka</p>\n<p>- Dr. Virginia Hardie</p>\n<p>- Dr. Arlyn Valencia (Neurologist)</p>\n<p>- Dr. George Tsao</p>\n<p>- Dr. Alexander Lee</p>\n<p>- Dr. Steven Olenchak</p>\n<p>- Dr. Dana Clark</p>\n<p>- Dr. Ruben Alexander</p>\n"},{"id":"s1c","h":"AM: Sample Process Guide: the First 5 Steps","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Here are the first 5 steps of the process guide as your sample. Feel free to format the guide according to your preference</b></p>\n<p><b>SENDING MEDLOR AND REQUEST FOR BILLS &amp; RECORDS</b></p>\n<p>1. Verify the Correct Client Case / Matter in SA: Before doing any work in SmartAdvocate, always ensure that you are on the correct client project or matter before proceeding.</p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Confirm the client’s full name and case number.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>Verify that you are inside the correct case/matter of the client in SmartAdvocate.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>If the client has multiple matters, verify the DOL to ensure you are working on the correct project.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span>For training demo purposes, you should narrate that you are verifying the correct matter, assuming the verification step even if you are using a training account or dummy matter.</span></p>\n<p>2. Check the assigned task in the TASK MENU of the client in Smart Advocate, or the task could be emailed by Case Manager or the Attorney, especially if it is urgent.</p>\n<p>3. Check the details of the task by double-clicking on it anywhere in the row, and you will find all the necessary information about your task in the DESCRIPTION BOX.</p>\n<p>copy and paste it into your notepad to avoid revisiting this section in case you forget some details.</p>\n<p>Take note of the name of the medical provider</p>\n<p>4. Go to the PLAINTIFF Section and click plaintiff&#x27;s name to be routed to its contact card or click the dropdown arrow beside the case number.</p>\n<p>Note the complete name, DOB, Home-Primary Phone Number, Home-Primary Address &amp; SSN.</p>\n<p>5. Kindly also obtain the  DOL of the client in the summary page.</p>\n<p><b>How to find the DOL/DOI/DOA</b></p>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day14/img/image51.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day14/img/image51.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"s1d","h":"AM: Gentle Reminders & SA Updates","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Gentle Reminders:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time Management &amp; Efficiency Metric:</b> The ideal time for completing the demo is 1 hour and 45 minutes. Any time beyond 1 hour and 45 minutes will result in a deduction from your performance rating. Please manage your time accordingly.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Preferred Document Tool:</b> For documents, please preferably use <b>Microsoft Word</b> to ensure compatibility with our templates and to avoid formatting or editing issues when working on the MedLOR.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>PDF Editor Requirement:</b> If you do not have Nitro Pro PDF Editor, make sure you have another PDF editor that is capable of merging files, adding text, and editing existing text. This will prevent issues during your demo and avoid wasting time addressing these issues during your demos. </span></p>\n<p><b>Please resolve any tool-related issues before your scheduled demo.</b> Do not wait until the demo starts to troubleshoot or install the necessary tools, as this may affect your completion time and result in an unnecessary deduction.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your cooperation and preparation.</p>\n<hr class=\"stars\">\n<p>FYI – Current SmartAdvocate (SA) Updates</p>\n<p><b>Please take note of the following current updates in Smart Advocate (SA) before proceeding with the demo.</b></p>\n<p><b>1. MEDS Tab Location Has Changed</b></p>\n<p>The MEDS tab is NO LONGER located under the PLAINTIFF section. It is now located under the GENERAL section.</p>\n<p>Therefore, for this demo, ALL THE TABS you will be using are located under the GENERAL section.</p>\n<p>You may still use the PLAINTIFF section if you need to access the client’s contact card by clicking the hyperlinked plaintiff’s name.</p>\n<p><b>2. Client Contact Card Has Been Updated.</b></p>\n<p>VLF has made changes to the client contact card.</p>\n<p>In the tutorial video, John Test Doe and the corresponding client/index information were used as the sample client for the training account. However, the details currently shown in the training account have been updated.</p>\n<p><b>For the DOCGEN DUMMY ACCOUNT training account, continue using the client name John Test Doe when completing the documents. However, use the current client index details shown in the updated contact card for all other information.</b></p>\n<p><b>NOTE: The current client name displayed in the training account is “I Test Doe.” For the purposes of this demo, use John Test Doe as the client name in your MedLOR and HIPAA documents, while using the updated client index details from the contact card.</b></p>\n<p><b>Important: Do not simply copy the information shown in the tutorial video. Always refer to the current contact card for the updated client details.</b></p>\n<p><b>3. Update the Client Information in Your Documents</b></p>\n<p>Because the current client details have changed, you will need to edit the applicable sections of your MedLOR and HIPAA documents to reflect the updated information.</p>\n<p>This portion may not have been demonstrated in the tutorial video, but it is an important part of the actual workflow.</p>\n<p><b>4. Why Is This Important?</b></p>\n<p>In actual tasks, there may be instances where updated client information – such as a phone number or address, is not automatically populated in a template, particularly when there is a system glitch or other issue.</p>\n<p>This is why you should always review and verify all information before finalizing a document, even when you are using a template or previously prepared information.</p>\n<p>Do not assume that information is correct simply because it was automatically populated. Always compare the document against the current information in SmartAdvocate and make the necessary corrections.</p>\n<p><b>Please be guided accordingly and make sure to incorporate these updates into the relevant sections of your process guide and apply them during the demo.</b></p>\n"},{"id":"s1e","h":"PM: Recorded Demonstration - Sending MedLOR (Medical Letter of Representation) and Requesting for Medical Bills & Records","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Demo Metrics</h4>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day14/img/image55.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day14/img/image55.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"14:s1-1\"></div>\n<h3>All trainees must be fully prepared to perform their scheduled demonstrations. Any missed demonstration due to unpreparedness will be considered a missed performance and will NOT be rescheduled under any circumstance.</h3>\n<h3>The only valid reason for rescheduling a demonstration is when the delay is due to a Training Team factor, such as lack of time during the session, unexpected scheduling conflicts initiated by the training team, or technical limitations.</h3>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Shadowing Session","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"14:s2-1\"></div>\n<p>Join your shadow buddy at the time your trainer posts in the training GC, and log the session with 👥 Shadowing log on this slide.</p>\n<p><b>Note: </b>If no shadowing buddy is available, recorded shadowing video/s will be provided to trainees instead.</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"15":{"day":15,"title":"Provider Communication Training","heading":"DAY 15: Provider Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Before Your Recorded Demonstration","of":"s1","html":"<p>Today is your recorded demonstration of sending the MedLOR and requesting medical bills &amp; records. Go over the tutorial video and your process guide before you record.</p>\n<p>Tutorial Video:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Tutorial Video: https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Oy2X1S9nokz5tqMm_P6nByqYaakvGDU/view?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n<p><b>Gentle Reminders:</b></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Time Management &amp; Efficiency Metric:</b> The ideal time for completing the demo is 1 hour and 45 minutes. Any time beyond 1 hour and 45 minutes will result in a deduction from your performance rating. Please manage your time accordingly.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>Preferred Document Tool:</b> For documents, please preferably use <b>Microsoft Word</b> to ensure compatibility with our templates and to avoid formatting or editing issues when working on the MedLOR.</span></p>\n<p class=\"li\" style=\"--lvl:0\"><span class=\"lbl\">•</span><span><b>PDF Editor Requirement:</b> If you do not have Nitro Pro PDF Editor, make sure you have another PDF editor that is capable of merging files, adding text, and editing existing text. This will prevent issues during your demo and avoid wasting time addressing these issues during your demos. </span></p>\n<p><b>Please resolve any tool-related issues before your scheduled demo.</b> Do not wait until the demo starts to troubleshoot or install the necessary tools, as this may affect your completion time and result in an unnecessary deduction.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your cooperation and preparation.</p>\n<h3>All trainees must be fully prepared to perform their scheduled demonstrations. Any missed demonstration due to unpreparedness will be considered a missed performance and will NOT be rescheduled under any circumstance.</h3>\n<h3>The only valid reason for rescheduling a demonstration is when the delay is due to a Training Team factor, such as lack of time during the session, unexpected scheduling conflicts initiated by the training team, or technical limitations.</h3>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"Entire Day: Recorded Demonstration - Sending MedLOR (Medical Letter of Representation) and Requesting for Medical Bills & Records","of":"s1","html":"<h3>Demo Metrics</h3>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day15/img/image55.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day15/img/image55.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Shadowing Session","html":"<p><b>Note: </b>If no shadowing buddy is available, recorded shadowing video/s will be provided to trainees instead.</p>\n<p>Join your shadow buddy at the time your trainer posts in the training GC, and log the session with 👥 Shadowing log on this slide.</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours</i></b></p>"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]},"16":{"day":16,"title":"Provider Communication Training","heading":"DAY 16: Provider Communication Training","slides":[{"id":"s1","h":"AM: Tutorial Video – Lien Balance Verification Request","of":"s1","html":"<p><b>Topic: Lien Balance Verification Request</b></p>\n<p>Tutorial Video: </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Tutorial Video: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wRXRh8TySsosyxurXzhtCYwbXDJyN9A9/view?usp\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wRXRh8TySsosyxurXzhtCYwbXDJyN9A9/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wRXRh8TySsosyxurXzhtCYwbXDJyN9A9/view?usp=sharing</a> </p>\n<p>NOTE: Please don&#x27;t forget to take down notes for your guide later.</p>\n"},{"id":"s1b","h":"AM: Notes for Your Guide","of":"s1","html":"<h4>Please add these in your notes. </h4>\n<p><b>Naming convention for Lien Balance Verification</b></p>\n<p>MED – Lien Holder(Provider) –  Lien Balance Verification mm.dd.yyyy (va’s first name)</p>\n<p><b>Note:</b>  For NPIM, always put the name of the doctor after the medical provider&#x27;s name.  </p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<p>MED - RDG(NPIM Dr. Fabito) - Lien Balance Verification 08.17.2022 (jane)</p>\n<p><b>-----------------</b></p>\n<p><b>Templates </b></p>\n<p>Report Format on Notes tab:</p>\n<p>Sent filename w/o va&#x27;s name. Saved in Meds and Docs tab. Thank you. (va&#x27;s first name)</p>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Highlight the filename, right click and paste the internal link. </p>\n<p>Report Format on Tasks tab:</p>\n<p>mm/dd/yyyy Sent LV request to <u>lien holder(medical provider)</u>. Saved in Meds and Docs tab. Thank you. (va&#x27;s first name)</p>\n<p><b>-----------------</b></p>\n<p><b>Sending request: E-mail/E-filing</b></p>\n<p>Subject Line:  </p>\n<p>Name of the client - Name of the lien holder(medical provider) - Request for Lien Verification</p>\n"},{"id":"s2","h":"PM: Demo and Shadowing","of":"s2","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"16:s2-1\"></div>\n<p>Please be reminded to type &#x27;done&#x27; here as soon as you are done watching the video and have finalized your process guide. Thank you.</p>\n<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"16:s2-2\"></div>\n<p>While waiting for your turn to perform, you may watch the following recorded demos below. Thank you.</p>\n<p>Sending Lien Balance Verification request using SA.     </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending Lien Balance Verification request using SA. https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q55zh\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q55zhsC-Oi2A1kQSo-CoBr3C7DsFmFmv/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q55zhsC-Oi2A1kQSo-CoBr3C7DsFmFmv/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Sending MedLOR using Filevine: </p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending MedLOR using Filevine: https://drive.google.com/file/d/11mvVFbtzbWIVcKM0XwVm_lp11_\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11mvVFbtzbWIVcKM0XwVm_lp11_5mbseR/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/11mvVFbtzbWIVcKM0XwVm_lp11_5mbseR/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending MedLOR using Filevine: https://drive.google.com/file/d/13DGgCl5S_FjCUBoj-Oo65_68lB\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/13DGgCl5S_FjCUBoj-Oo65_68lBrwZz3u/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/13DGgCl5S_FjCUBoj-Oo65_68lBrwZz3u/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>Sending Lien Balance Verification request using Filevine:</p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending Lien Balance Verification request using Filevine: https://drive.google.com/file/d/\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BAp24F_I3JgycQfZK0-6lZdmsYSVRS0-/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BAp24F_I3JgycQfZK0-6lZdmsYSVRS0-/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending Lien Balance Verification request using Filevine: https://drive.google.com/file/d/\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zPnBl5qN4ltX7GBJefTxg5SlHwTi-EJU/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zPnBl5qN4ltX7GBJefTxg5SlHwTi-EJU/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p><a class=\"viewer-link\" data-kind=\"video\" data-title=\"Sending Lien Balance Verification request using Filevine: https://drive.google.com/file/d/\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rLEotcYvyl4-oXBGJNKgnwKez1McCb4L/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rLEotcYvyl4-oXBGJNKgnwKez1McCb4L/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n"},{"id":"s2b","h":"PM: Before Your Demo: Rules, Metrics & Time Limit","of":"s2","html":"<div class=\"trainer-slot\" data-slot=\"16:s2-3\"></div>\n<h3>All trainees must be fully prepared to perform their scheduled demonstrations. Any missed demonstration due to unpreparedness will be considered a missed performance and will NOT be rescheduled under any circumstance.</h3>\n<p>The only valid reason for rescheduling a demonstration is when the delay is due to a Training Team factor, such as lack of time during the session, unexpected scheduling conflicts initiated by the training team, or technical limitations.</p>\n<h4>Demo Metrics</h4>\n<div class=\"shots\"><figure><a href=\"/ft/day16/img/image53.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"/ft/day16/img/image53.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></div>\n<p>@everyone</p>\n<p>Please be informed that for the last metric of your LV Demo, Time Management &amp; Efficiency, the ideal completion time is 45 minutes. Going beyond the allotted time will result in a significant deduction under this metric. Please be guided and manage your time accordingly.</p>\n<p><b><i>*** Free Communication Upskill for 1 or 1 ½ hours </i></b></p>\n"},{"id":"to-be-added","h":"To be added","placeholder":true,"html":"<div class=\"ftdd-ph ftdd-ph-blank\"><span class=\"ftdd-ph-ic\">📌</span><div><b>More is on its way</b><p>Your trainer will add the rest of today’s material here. Until then, follow the slides before this one and the training GC.</p></div></div>"}]}};
